{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D(198|260|354|439|543|647|655|664|665|67[6-9]|68[0-8])'\"\\\\b|39\\\\.29' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"2559:## D198 · 2026-10-27 · A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force\n3049:## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n3685:## D354 · 2026-11-03 · Steps 3 and 4 (opening and matching questions, judging them) are frozen as `poc-v108` runs them, after three draws on the frozen extraction\n4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n6589:## D543 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the cold reflection on the lean path: D518 stands with its reasons, the choice of system is not made in Alex's place, and no investigation is opened (reflection council consensus)\n8892:## D647 · 2026-11-16 · The Opus trial reads \"inconclusive\": fewer failures, one real new failure, a sharp reader-family split, astra-level cost\n8912:- **Spending:** D439 stands at about $39.29 of $40, including run-1's $0.026.\n9116:## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\n9383:## D664 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: no budget needed for the comparison; D658 waits; the council determines whether the six lines still make sense and what decides readiness\n9398:## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n10007:## D676 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison: the new system loses for two known mechanisms; keep the old system; the outcome was computable before the run (council consensus)\n10042:## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n10061:## D678 · 2026-11-19 · Merge design (council consensus): the old system opens questions, the clean system reads and organises evidence, the same judge answers; a 12-article test awaits Alex's approval\n10079:## D679 · 2026-11-19 · Alex lifts D677's paid-send stop for the merge test only; the test runs on 70 articles, two old draws, two judging arms, under a $5 ledger\n10102:## D680 · 2026-11-19 · Merge test closed (council e): delivery verified, the registered test did not pass (P2's proxy clause and V missed)\n10125:## D681 · 2026-11-20 · Alex opens the hybrid system's build and test; phase 1 is a new judge version (J2) for the judge's reasoning errors\n10150:## D682 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681 (council): J2a and J2b retired; the carried previous conclusion is the lead mechanism; a separating test on complete evidence\n10177:## D683 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681/D682 (council H): the removal of the previous conclusion is not accepted; one presentation-only test goes to Alex\n10199:## D684 · 2026-11-20 · Under D683: Alex approves the presentation-only test and hands the iteration to Claude (\"那你自己持续迭代\")\n10212:## D685 · 2026-11-20 · Under D684 (councils I–K): the fresh test cannot be fed; H1 fails its diagnostic; the judge line pauses within D198; phase 2 (opening) starts\n10240:## D686 · 2026-11-20 · Under D685 (council L): the opening census; D382 goes to Alex first\n10263:## D687 · 2026-11-20 · Alex: in the hybrid, a company's own material figure gets its own question\n10274:## D688 · 2026-11-20 · Under D687 (council M): no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone; to Alex, keep old and pause the hybrid's release line\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DAR