{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\\\\\"'$40|39'\"\\\\.29|phase1b|\\\\\"'$2'\"\\\\.64|\\\\\"'$0'\"\\\\.36' docs/DECISIONS-log.md | tail -55; rg --files poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20 | rg -v '/(probe|account)/' | sed -n '1,150p'; tail -n 10 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"2534:  - **Helios first shipments (A14), Intelligent Cloud FY2027 (A13), CoreWeave FY2026 revenue (A12): the model's.** Each is a stated number or date (\"initial shipments on track to begin later this quarter\"; Intelligent Cloud guided to $40.95–41.25bn, Azure +45%; revenue guidance raised to $12.4–13.2bn). The three share one shape: the first call of a company in the window, where the model opened one or two theses and stopped. That is the first-contact pattern v13 tried (D192: +0.7 must-open, +3.7 must-not-open), so it is a known limit of v12, recorded here, not an open arm.\n3052:- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\n3054:- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n3067:- First measurement on the frozen gold (`score-r4-identity.txt`, arm 4, three draws, judging-v5): judged questions agreeing 13/19, 15/18, 12/17; the lookup baseline (the rung containing the gold's reference figure) 9/15, 8/14, 8/14; always-neutral 5/11, 5/10, 5/10. Disagreeing in every draw: FY2027 total revenue (gold $400–435 billion, judge neutral by consensus lookup) and Vera CPU revenue (gold $8–18 billion, judge the top rung on management's $20 billion at face value); in two of three: the financing-commitments total (gold $25–60 billion, judge $10–20 billion). Never judged in any draw: NVIDIA's own capex (q12); the operating margin in two draws (q10): evidence never reached them, counted apart as \"no judgement\". The new judge (`judging-v6`, D260) has no run to score yet; a run on `poc-v90` is Alex's call.\n3073:- Proof on the stored requests of the questions whose arm-4 judgement differed from the gold (`proof-judging-v7a.txt`, `proof-judging-v7.txt`; one send each, cents): total revenue rung 3 → 2 (about $421 billion from the guided growth on FY2026's base; gold $400–435 billion), Data Center 3 → 2 (about $372 billion; gold $370–400 billion), Vera CPU 1 → 2 ($12 to below $20 billion, the target discounted for the volume not in hand; gold $8–18 billion), DRAM prices 3 → 2 (about +15%; gold +10–35%), financing total stays 4 ($33.5–39.8 billion; gold $25–60 billion), the Ohio guarantee stays Yes; China share stays below 1% in draw 1, consistent with that draw's H200 theme judged No (the gold has the authorization likely and the share 1–8%; the consistency clause ties the share to the theme, so it moves with it). Six of the seven re-sent questions now land in the gold's band; the end-to-end agreement under judging-v7 needs a run on `poc-v91`, which is Alex's call. A placement gap seen on the way: the Vera CPU question never held the fall-launch statement (filed under the Rubin launch questions), so the judge could not count selling quarters from evidence; the default-discount clause covers it, the filing is a D2 class to count.\n3706:  none of the frozen ones (it went to the total-revenue, data-center and accelerator-share questions), and the judge then chose below $40bn\n3796:- Amendment, 17:05. Alex, on seeing an empty thesis in the front end (\"why is this here? there is no evidence and why is this a thesis\"; then \"你直接把它移除，这是我们自己的失误\"): v68, \"What stand-alone CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for calendar 2027?\", opened on the run's last day by the succession rule (D168: same quantity, next period, after v24) from one statement (\"$20 billion in 2026 and more than $40 billion in 2027\"); the writer linked that statement to v7 and v24 (as a repeat of the $20 billion piece) and not to the successor it opened, so v68 stood with no evidence and, judging running only on arrivals, no judgement. Class: 1 of 69 theses with no evidence; 1 of 2 successions (v9 after v8 has 59 pieces). The sealed folder stays untouched; the front end, the API and the page build now read `poc/data/served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite`, the same ledger with v68's rows removed (views, view_keys, rungs, successions, view_switches, views_fts; the append-only triggers dropped in that copy only; its README lists this). The writer gap (a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the successor) is an open defect in `writing.py` for the next slice.\n4875:- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n4883:- **Amended 2026-11-13 (council round mj-5, `council/mj-codex-5.md`: \"Council position: consensus on (a)\"):** the 11 jobs the $2.0 ceiling never sent are sent alone, same requests, under a $1.2 completion ceiling (a recorded departure from D440's step ceiling; the $40 total unchanged), before any diagnostic answer is read; the combined sample must hold 18 per arm per draw, or the diagnostic is inconclusive.\n5518:- **To Alex:** the lines and the budget (the cost passes the $40 ceiling Claude set while he was away).\n5857:  did not receive NVIDIA's revenue opportunity per gigawatt (about $25 billion with Blackwell, $40 billion with Vera Rubin), stated\n5913:  this period stay within D439's ceiling of $40 at published rates in total (Claude's setting), each paid step with its own ceiling\n5933:  before it about $18.4 of $40. The result goes to the council before any further step. Nothing in the system changes.\n5938:  $0.0093 at the published rates (ceiling $0.25); spend recorded under D439 about $18.41 of $40. All six answers are \"yes\"; two\n6020:  delivery line stays paused (D511); production stays the default. Spend recorded under D439: about $18.41 of $40; the lean path\n6464:  matching engine recorded \"part of\", 1.00): the total's conclusion carried the year's consensus ($406.05 billion from 09-23,\n6701:  attempts, $0.0022 of a $0.05 ceiling; spend recorded under D439 about $18.43 of $40): the request of the answer-choice step\n6774:  direction at most $3.9522 after the run, under D439 at most about $22.38 of $40. A line the third readers leave open is\n6881:  or cut attempts charged at their reservations); paid calls under D439 about $22.10 of $40. D544's $5 checkpoint is reached\n7116:- **Spend:** within D439's $40 ceiling (about $22.10 recorded before this run).\n7158:     total spend stays within D439's $40.\n7213:  baseline warns on 17 of 22 failed and 21 of 23 passed. Ceiling $0.45 (bound $0.403), within D439's $40 (about $26.0 spent). It\n7440:  - Planted controls: 6 of 6 marks as expected. The third readers split by family on H (19 of 30). Spend $0.108; about $26.18 of $40\n7537:  - Spend $0.15; D439 about $26