{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '1,272p'; cat poc/config/poc-v118.json\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"06-views.md step 7: one re-judging round. Open views whose reading changed are judged in dependency order, each\n     2\tonce; a view whose conclusion changed adds its open dependants. The model reads the evidence in force (with each\n     3\treplaced predecessor), the dependencies' current conclusions and its own last conclusion (for comparison only).\n     4\tCode checks every citation and that a rung move or a first judgement says changed; one retry, then the item fails.\n     5\t\n     6\tThe request is judging-v7 (D354, frozen with steps 3 and 4): no other version is built, and a configuration that names another is\n     7\trefused before any call. Every answer is stored in the canonical vocabulary.\n     8\t\n     9\tThe theme block (D191, D195): an asset thesis is judged with every open, judged theme thesis in view and answers, in theme_pushes,\n    10\twhich way each theme it weighed pushes it; theme theses are judged before asset theses in a round, and a theme judgement that says\n    11\tchanged queues every open asset thesis with evidence in force, once. The round's queue is derived from the ledger (the day's changed\n    12\tviews, the dependants of views judged at this sequence number with a changed conclusion, and the asset theses a changed theme queues),\n    13\tso a resumed round recovers what an earlier commit had queued.\n    14\t\n    15\tThe evidence in view (D198): a judgement reads the arrivals and the basis among the evidence in force, not everything in force.\n    16\t\n    17\tThe reference (D260): the rung is the forecast the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects\n    18\t(consensus, guidance, the stated plan); the answer states the reference and the outcome the evidence implies, both stored beside the\n    19\trung, and an empty one is refused.\"\"\"\n    20\timport dataclasses\n    21\timport json\n    22\timport re\n    23\t\n    24\tfrom .. import config, model, vocabulary\n    25\tfrom . import store\n    26\t\n    27\tPUSHES = vocabulary.PUSHES\n    28\tSUPPORTED_VERSIONS = ('judging-v7',)   # D354: the frozen judging prompt\n    29\tREADINGS = 5                      # a piece is shown in the thesis's first five judgements after it arrives\n    30\tBASIS = 10                        # and while one of the last ten judgements cited it\n    31\tTHEME_REASONS_CHARS = 300\n    32\tUPDATED_MARK = 'updated since this thesis was last judged'\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef require_supported(prompt_version):\n    36\t    \"\"\"Refuses a judging prompt version this code does not build, before any request is made.\"\"\"\n    37\t    if prompt_version not in SUPPORTED_VERSIONS:\n    38\t        raise ValueError(f'judging {prompt_version!r} is not built; this code builds only {\", \".join(SUPPORTED_VERSIONS)} (D354)')\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef evidence_in_view(conn, view_id):\n    42\t    \"\"\"(the pieces a judgement of this thesis reads, how many pieces in force are not shown): the arrivals (linked after the\n    43\t    READINGS-th most recent judgement, or all when there are fewer) and the basis (cited by one of the last BASIS judgements),\n    44\t    both among the evidence in force.\"\"\"\n    45\t    in_force = store.evidence_in_force(conn, view_id)\n    46\t    recent = store.recent_judgements(conn, view_id, BASIS)\n    47\t    arrivals_after = recent[READINGS - 1]['seq'] if len(recent) >= READINGS else -1\n    48\t    basis = {evidence_id for j in recent for evidence_id in j['cites']}\n    49\t    linked_at = {r['evidence_id']: r['seq'] for r in conn.execute('select evidence_id, seq from evidence_links where view_id=?', (view_id,))}\n    50\t    shown = [p for p in in_force if linked_at.get(p['evidence_id'], -1) > arrivals_after or p['evidence_id'] in basis]\n    51\t    return shown, len(in_force) - len(shown)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef schema_for(prompt_version):\n    55\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n    56\t    pushes = PUSHES\n    57\t    schema = {\n    58\t        'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False,\n    59\t        'required': ['rung', 'reasons', 'cites', 'cites_views', 'pushes', 'changed', 'why_changed'],\n    60\t        'properties': {\n    61\t            'rung': {'type': 'integer'}, 'reasons': {'type': 'string'},\n    62\t            'cites': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}}, 'cites_views': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}},\n    63\t            'pushes': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['evidence_id', 'push'],\n    64\t                                                  'properties': {'evidence_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}},\n    65\t            'changed': {'type': 'boolean'}, 'why_changed': {'type': 'string'},\n    66\t        },\n    67\t    }\n    68\t    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n    69\t    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n    70\t                                                                       'properties': {'view_id': {'type': 'string'}, 'push': {'type': 'string', 'enum': pushes}}}}\n    71\t    schema['required'][1:1] = STANCE_FIELDS           # after rung: the reference and the implied outcome are written before the reasons\n    72\t    schema['properties'].update({field: {'type': 'string'} for field in STANCE_FIELDS})\n    73\t    return schema\n    74\t\n    75\t\n    76\tdef themes_in_force(conn, view_id):\n    77\t    \"\"\"The theme block of an asset thesis: every open theme thesis with a current state, with its rung label and whether a\n    78\t    changed conclusion was recorded after this thesis's last judgement. Empty for a theme thesis.\"\"\"\n    79\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n    80\t        return []\n    81\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n    82\t    out = []\n    83\t    for row in conn.execute(\"select view_id from views where object_kind='theme' order by view_id\"):\n    84\t        theme_id = row['view_id']\n    85\t        state = store.current_state(conn, theme_id)\n    86\t        if not state or not store.is_open(conn, theme_id):\n    87\t            continue\n    88\t        updated = bool(last) and bool(conn.execute('select 1 from judgements where view_id=? and changed=1 and judgement_id>? limit 1',\n    89\t                                                   (theme_id, last['judgement_id'])).fetchone())\n    90\t        rung = store.rungs_of(conn, theme_id)[state['rung'] - 1]\n    91\t        out.append({'view_id': theme_id, 'view': store.view(conn, theme_id), 'state': state, 'rung_label': rung['label'], 'updated': updated})\n    92\t    return out\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\tSTANCE_FIELDS = ['reference', 'implied_outcome']   # D260: what the market expects, and the figure or date the evidence implies\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\tclass JudgementRefused(Exception):\n    99\t    pass\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef topological(conn, view_ids):\n   103\t    \"\"\"Dependencies first: a view comes after every view it depends on that is also in the set.\"\"\"\n   104\t    remaining = list(dict.fromkeys(view_ids))\n   105\t    ordered, placed = [], set()\n   106\t    while remaining:\n   107\t        progressed = False\n   108\t        for view_id in list(remaining):\n   109\t            deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   110\t            if deps.isdisjoint(set(remaining) - {view_id}) or deps <= placed:\n   111\t                ordered.append(view_id)\n   112\t                placed.add(view_id)\n   113\t                remaining.remove(view_id)\n   114\t                progressed = True\n   115\t        if not progressed:                 # a cycle slipped through: keep going in the given order\n   116\t            ordered.extend(remaining)\n   117\t            break\n   118\t    return ordered\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\tdef _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes=(), hidden=0):\n   122\t    \"\"\"hidden: how many pieces in force are not shown.\"\"\"\n   123\t    lines = [f'Thesis {view_id} ({v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}',\n   124\t             'Ladder: ' + ' / '.join(f'rung {r[\"position\"]} {r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in rungs), '',\n   125\t             f'[Evidence in view under this thesis, {len(pieces)} items]']\n   126\t    if hidden:\n   127\t        lines.append(f'[Not shown: {hidden} more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]')\n   128\t    for p in pieces:\n   129\t        src = p['sources'][0] if p['sources'] else {}\n   130\t        lines.append(f'- {p[\"evidence_id\"]} [{p[\"tier\"]}; {p[\"speaker\"]}; original source {p[\"original_who\"]} {p[\"original_day\"]}; from {src.get(\"input_id\")} {src.get(\"publication_day\")}] {p[\"one_line\"]}\\n    Quote: {p[\"quote\"][:400]}')\n   131\t        if p.get('replaced'):\n   132\t            lines.append(f'    It replaces {p[\"replaced\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"replaced\"][\"original_day\"]}): {p[\"replaced\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   133\t        if p.get('same_as'):\n   134\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as {\", \".join(p[\"same_as\"])}; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.')\n   135\t        if p.get('revises'):\n   136\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   137\t    if deps:\n   138\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   139\t        for d in deps:\n   140\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   141\t            if not target:\n   142\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   143\t                continue\n   144\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   145\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   146\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   147\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   148\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   149\t    if themes:\n   150\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   151\t        for theme in themes:\n   152\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   153\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   154\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   155\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   156\t    if last:\n   157\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   158\t    else:\n   159\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   160\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   161\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   162\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   163\t    return lines\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   167\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   168\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   169\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   170\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   171\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   172\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   173\t    lines = _lines_english(conn, view_id, v, rungs, pieces, deps, last, themes_in_force(conn, view_id), hidden=hidden)\n   174\t    with open(config.prompt_path(prompt_version + '.txt'), encoding='utf-8') as handle:\n   175\t        return handle.read(), '\\n'.join(lines)\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\tdef retry_note(errors):\n   179\t    return '\\n\\nThe code returned the previous answer because: ' + '; '.join(errors) + '\\nCorrect it and answer again, citing only the listed ids.'\n   180\t\n   181\t\n   182\tdef themes_shown_in(request_text):\n   183\t    \"\"\"The theme ids of the block a request carried: the ids the answer may name, whatever the ledger says now.\"\"\"\n   184\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Themes in force, ', 1)\n   185\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (v\\d+) \\(', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\tdef evidence_shown_in(request_text):\n   189\t    \"\"\"The evidence ids the request listed: the ids the answer may cite and push.\"\"\"\n   190\t    block = request_text.split('\\n[Evidence in ', 1)\n   191\t    return set(re.findall(r'^- (e\\d+) \\[', block[1].split('\\n\\n[', 1)[0], re.M)) if len(block) == 2 else set()\n   192\t\n   193\t\n   194\tdef check_answer(conn, view_id, data, request_text=None):\n   195\t    \"\"\"request_text: the user message that was sent, so theme and evidence ids are checked against what it carried (a theme may have\n   196\t    closed or opened since); without it, against what the ledger would show now.\"\"\"\n   197\t    errors = []\n   198\t    shown = themes_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {theme['view_id'] for theme in themes_in_force(conn, view_id)}\n   199\t    named = []\n   200\t    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n   201\t        if entry['view_id'] in named:\n   202\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n   203\t        elif entry['view_id'] not in shown:\n   204\t            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is not a theme in force shown to {view_id}')\n   205\t        named.append(entry['view_id'])\n   206\t    # the closed set is what the request showed (D198), read from the text that was sent, else computed from the ledger\n   207\t    allowed = evidence_shown_in(request_text) if request_text is not None else {p['evidence_id'] for p in evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)[0]}\n   208\t    not_allowed = lambda e: f'{e} is not among the evidence shown to {view_id}'\n   209\t    bad_push = lambda e: f'push on {e} which was not shown to {view_id}'\n   210\t    deps = {d['resolved_to'] for d in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id) if d['resolved_to']}\n   211\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   212\t    if not 1 <= data['rung'] <= len(rungs):\n   213\t        errors.append(f'rung {data[\"rung\"]} outside 1..{len(rungs)}')\n   214\t    for cited in data['cites']:\n   215\t        if cited not in allowed:\n   216\t            errors.append(not_allowed(cited))\n   217\t    for cited in data['cites_views']:\n   218\t        if cited not in deps:\n   219\t            errors.append(f'{cited} is not a dependency of {view_id}')\n   220\t    for push in data['pushes']:\n   221\t        if push['evidence_id'] not in allowed:\n   222\t            errors.append(bad_push(push['evidence_id']))\n   223\t    for field in STANCE_FIELDS:\n   224\t        if not str(data.get(field) or '').strip():\n   225\t            errors.append(f'{field} is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies')\n   226\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   227\t    if last is None and not data['changed']:\n   228\t        errors.append('first judgement must say changed')\n   229\t    if last is not None and last['rung'] != data['rung'] and not data['changed']:\n   230\t        errors.append(f'rung moved from {last[\"rung\"]} to {data[\"rung\"]} but changed is false')\n   231\t    return errors\n   232\t\n   233\t\n   234\tdef _record(conn, cfg, view_id, seq, item, answer):\n   235\t    data = vocabulary.judgement_answer(answer.data)\n   236\t    judgement_id = store.insert(conn, 'judgements', view_id=view_id, seq=seq, input_id=item['input_id'], rung=data['rung'],\n   237\t                                reasons=data['reasons'], cited_evidence_json=json.dumps(data['cites']), cited_views_json=json.dumps(data['cites_views']),\n   238\t                                pushes_json=json.dumps(data['pushes'], ensure_ascii=False), changed=1 if data['changed'] else 0,\n   239\t                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\n   240\t                                reference=data.get('reference'), implied_outcome=data.get('implied_outcome'),\n   241\t                                why_changed=data['why_changed'], config_checksum=cfg.checksum, call_id=answer.call_id,\n   242\t                                request_sha256=answer.request_sha256, publication_day=item['publication_day'])\n   243\t    conn.commit()\n   244\t    return {'view_id': view_id, 'judgement_id': judgement_id, 'rung': data['rung'], 'changed': data['changed'], 'cost': answer.cost_usd, 'cached': answer.cached}\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\tJUDGE_WORKERS = 32     # a day's round is up to 40 judgements of about 16 s each in two dependency levels (themes, then assets); 32 at a time makes a round about two calls long (2026-11-02)\n   248\t\n   249\t\n   250\tdef upstream(conn, view_id):\n   251\t    \"\"\"Every view this one depends on, directly or through its dependencies.\"\"\"\n   252\t    seen, stack = set(), [view_id]\n   253\t    while stack:\n   254\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, stack.pop()):\n   255\t            target = dep['resolved_to']\n   256\t            if target and target not in seen:\n   257\t                seen.add(target)\n   258\t                stack.append(target)\n   259\t    return seen\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\tdef open_asset_views(conn):\n   263\t    return [v for v in store.open_views(conn) if store.view(conn, v)['object_kind'] != 'theme']\n   264\t\n   265\t\n   266\tdef queued_by_change(conn, view_id):\n   267\t    \"\"\"What a changed conclusion of this view queues: its dependants and, for a theme thesis, every open asset thesis. The one rule,\n   268\t    read for a live judgement and for the judgements a resumed round finds committed.\"\"\"\n   269\t    queued = store.dependants_of(conn, view_id)\n   270\t    if store.view(conn, view_id)['object_kind'] == 'theme':\n   271\t        queued = queued + open_asset_views(conn)\n   272\t    return queued\n{\n  \"version\": \"poc-v118\",\n  \"_note\": \"Field-free configuration derived from poc-v117.json; all active model and prompt settings remain unchanged.\",\n  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n  \"search_top_n\": 10,\n  \"extraction\": {\n    \"T1\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T1-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    },\n    \"T2\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T2-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    },\n    \"T3\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T3-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    },\n    \"T4\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T4-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    },\n    \"T5\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T5-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    },\n    \"T6\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T6-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    },\n    \"T7\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T7-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    },\n    \"T8\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T8-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    },\n    \"T10\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T10-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    },\n    \"T11\": {\n      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n      \"prompt_version\": \"T11-v74i\",\n      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    }\n  },\n  \"matching\": {\n    \"model\": \"jev-1.14.0\",\n    \"prompt_version\": \"matching-v3\",\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 12000,\n    \"engine\": \"jev\"\n  },\n  \"rejudging\": {\n    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    \"prompt_version\": \"judging-v7\",\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n  },\n  \"final_verdict\": {\n    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    \"prompt_version\": \"verdict-v0\",\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n  },\n  \"idea\": {\n    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    \"prompt_version\": \"idea-v11\",\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"none\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n  },\n  \"collision\": {\n    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    \"prompt_version\": \"collision-v2\",\n    \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2559,2583p;3049,3064p;3685,3695p;6589,6614p;9116,9142p;9383,9400p;10042,10061p'; cat docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/reflection-k-codex.md; sed -n '23,39p' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/reflection-k-claude.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2559,2583p;3049,3064p;3685,3695p;6589,6614p;9116,9142p;9383,9400p;10042,10061p'; cat docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/reflection-k-codex.md; sed -n '23,39p' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/reflection-k-claude.md\"","aggregated_output":"  2559\t## D198 · 2026-10-27 · A judgement reads the evidence in view, not everything in force\n  2560\t\n  2561\t- Alex, 2026-10-27, on the finding that evidence in force grows without bound (v6, NVIDIA FY2027 Data Center revenue: 574 pieces after six weeks, 415 never cited by any of its 33 judgements; 40 of 316 judge requests over 30k tokens, max 67k; judging 38% of spend and rising; the run's stall came from enumerating 300+ ids): \"这是什么问题你深度思考之后改\".\n  2562\t- What the problem is (design: `docs/research/2026-10-27-evidence-in-view/design.md`): two mechanisms. (1) Extraction links wide: `role-v14.txt` says \"every statement and number is, by default, evidence linked to a shown thesis\" and also \"link only to the thesis it directly concerns; omit statements with no thesis\"; the model attaches every business mention to the broadest thesis (2.5 pieces per item on v6; a liquid-cooling note, a SuperPOD purchase, a rack R&D story). Not changed here; the prompt audit is reported to Alex as the next slice. (2) Judging-v4 reads everything in force every time (\"Rejudge from all evidence currently in force\"); an analyst keeps what his view rests on and reads what arrived.\n  2563\t- Decided: from judging-v5 (`poc-v30`) a judgement of a thesis is shown, of its evidence in force, the arrivals (pieces linked after the thesis's fifth most recent judgement, READINGS = 5; everything when it has fewer) and the basis (pieces cited by one of its last ten judgements, BASIS = 10). The rest stays in force in the ledger; the request names the count (\"[Not shown: N more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them]\"); the answer may cite and push only shown ids, checked against the request that was sent (`judging.evidence_shown_in`, as the theme block is). Nothing leaves the ledger; the repeat / replace / new rules, \"in force\", the rejudgement triggers, eligibility, the theme block and dependencies are unchanged. Gated on the prompt version: v4 ledgers and configurations read in force as before.\n  2564\t- Measured ($0, `census.py`, two ledgers): among judgements after a thesis's first, the rule would have hidden 1.5% (nvda-3m) and 1.1% (r5) of the citations the judge actually made (22 of 325 and 7 of 261 judgements lose one cite, mostly third-party risk mentions listed in a \"pull the other way\" sentence); shown mean 95 and 109 pieces where in force averaged 225 and 178. Tighter rules hid 16% (cited last time + new since) or kept growing (ever cited + three readings). Arm beside control (`ab.py`, $0.03): v6, v11, v22 from the same ledger state, v4 fresh against v5: the same rung and `changed` on all three, reasons consistent, request tokens 76,476 → 12,516, 53,151 → 11,204, 25,806 → 8,425. Tests: `tests/test_evidence_in_view.py` (4, red first); suite 199.\n  2565\t- Applied to the three-month run at a day boundary: 2026-08-18 finished under `poc-v29` on the serial path (the parallel runner refuses a half-done day after a code change), `poc-v30` from 2026-08-19. Prompt `judging-v5` is `judging-v4` with the first rule reworded (2,264 → 2,437 characters; the growth is the sentence that says what is not shown and who carries it).\n  2566\t- Also in this slice, from the stall at 2026-08-07: a code-refused judgement answer is retired from the archive's lookup (`model.Archive.retire`; the row stays; schema-refused and malformed rows already carried a suffix), so a resume re-samples instead of replaying the refused answer; and the request's closing line names a closed set that exists (\"cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis\"; \"a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views\"): 4 of the run's 5 retried first answers had put theme ids into cites_views.\n  2567\t\n  2568\t## D199 · 2026-10-27 · One extraction call stays; its gate rule becomes decidable and the empty-answer exit goes (v16, poc-v32)\n  2569\t\n  2570\t- Alex, on the instability trace: \"不这个一次一定是可以搞过的 → 读明白，抽取 … 这一定是prompt 的问题，你如果再拆成两步这个消耗的luna calls 太多了\"; then \"你要反思自己的错误，然后下去改然后马上测试啊，不要一直diverge scope\". The two-call design (`docs/research/2026-10-27-two-step-extraction/design.md`, two review rounds) is recorded and not built.\n  2571\t- Found ([log](research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md)): the run's 493 empty extraction answers in 1,553 calls (32%; 65% of the first week's items) were the model following the written rules: \"every statement is, by default, evidence\" against \"link only to the thesis it directly concerns … omit statements with no thesis\", decided once per page, so a customer, partner or product page was omitted whole (asked directly, the model names that rule: a national lab buying Vera Rubin CPU servers \"describes a customer project, not NVIDIA's reported sales\"). The five-send benchmarks before this were sent with an alphabetised schema (the archive stores sorted keys; production sends the dict as built) and overstated the empties; in production order no send of three articles was empty. A second mistake stopped the first week test: code edited while the parallel runner was mid-day.\n  2572\t- Decided: extraction v16 (`role-v16.txt`: one rule, \"a statement is evidence to each shown thesis whose answer its fact or figure makes more or less likely\", with the customer/supplier/competitor/regulator and policy cases and the omit cases; the closing line \"Return empty arrays only for a page with no business content\", `extraction.EMPTY_LINE_FROM`; v12's admission reasons, `V12_REASON_VERSIONS`). `poc-v32.json` is the configuration. Measured on the same 98 items of 2026-07-01..07 against the paused run (v12, whole pages): empty handovers 65% → 32%, the model's own empties 55 → 8, evidence per item 1.1 → 2.7, candidates 9 → 11, week cost $0.22. v17 (`poc-v33`, an account per mandatory paragraph in the same call) held the piece set across sends (A3: Jaccard 0.6–0.8 against 0.4–0.5) but tripled the pieces with court-case minutiae and opened 5 theses where v16 opened 11, at twice the extraction and matching cost: refuted for production, kept as the record of the shape.\n  2573\t- The three-month run restarts from 2026-07-01 with poc-v32 on the cleaned database (D256) in `poc/data/english-v32-nvda-3m-2026-10-27/`; the poc-v29/v30 run stays paused and untouched. Open, named: links read widely (every piece to three or four theses; D198's \"links wide\"), candidates for product and gaming news (no thesis list entry fits them), the cold start's \"no thesis fits\" drops.\n  2574\t\n  2575\t- Amendment, 2026-10-27 23:20: Alex stopped the restarted run (\"我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？\") and asked for the prompt to be read and fixed, with examples (\"什么叫重要陈述，你也没给例子\"). Arms B1–B6 ([log](research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md) §10–17) rewrote the role as the model reads it: evidence first; four kinds of material statement with examples; a walk over the whole page (\"a page with eight such statements yields eight evidence items\"); a reject list with examples; links decided statement by statement; a rumour bears on a thesis as a confirmed statement does; T8's reading block narrowed to forecasts, ratings, targets and cited figures. Extraction v18 (`role-v18.txt`, `categories-v18.json`, `poc-v34.json`) supersedes v16 as the candidate configuration: on six articles sent five times each every material statement is present in every send; at scale (243 items of the run, one send each) 2% of answers are empty against 32% under v12 and 7–8 material statements come out per page, of which the theses that exist absorb 18% in the first week and 48% in the last. v17 and the two-call design stay refuted and unbuilt. The restarted run (`english-v32-nvda-3m-2026-10-27`, $0.215, 119 items) is paused; whether a run resumes, and with poc-v34, is Alex's call.\n  2576\t\n  2577\t## D200 · 2026-10-27 · Extraction v18 (`poc-v34`) is the production default\n  2578\t\n  2579\t- Alex, after the step 1 verdict (D199 amendment): \"is step one and step two done? … whatever latest fixed version that you have, it just needs to be on production for these two. Do it, and then we move to step three and four.\"\n  2580\t- Decided: `poc/config/poc-v34.json` (extraction T*-v18; matching, collision judge and judging as `poc-v30`) is the replay default (`scripts/replay.py --config`, README). Evidence: the arms B3–B6 and the two extraction-only scale tests in the [log](research/2026-10-27-single-call/log.md) §12–17 (243 items, 4 empty answers against 32% under v12, 7–8 material statements per page), recounted from the scratch archive before this decision.\n  2581\t- Acceptance on the product's own path: one week (2026-07-01..07, NVDA, cleaned database) replayed through extraction, matching and judging with `poc-v34` in `poc/data/english-v34-nvda-week-2026-10-27/`, compared with the v16 week (`compare_week.py`). The result is appended to the log; a defect found there is diagnosed under §1 before any further change.\n  2582\t- Step 2 on the review page (the complete retrieval entry point of D250, main branch) is verified as a component and has no production consumer until step 3 (question selection) exists; nothing of it goes to production in this decision. The paused runs (`english-v29/v30`, `english-v32`) stay paused; whether a three-month run resumes with `poc-v34` is Alex's call.\n  2583\t- Found while switching the default, before the acceptance run: `extraction.ACCOUNT_FROM = 17` made v18 send v17's per-paragraph account shape in production, while arms B3–B6 and both scale tests were sent with the flat shape (`arm.py` restores the stored request and replaces only the role, the closing line and T8's reading block). The harness bytes were not the production bytes (AGENTS §5). Fixed at the owner: `ACCOUNT_VERSIONS = (17,)` and `extraction.accounts(version)`; test `test_v18_sends_the_flat_answer_shape…` (red on the old code, green after); the production `poc-v34` request now equals the scale test's bytes for all 243 items (system, schema keys and evidence item, user text from the item header). Suite 205 pass; preflight exit 0.\n  3049\t## D260 · 2026-11-02 · A judgement is a forecast against a reference: the rung the evidence in force makes most likely, judged against what the market expects; the answer states the reference and the implied outcome (judging-v6)\n  3050\t\n  3051\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, asked whether the judge's stance should stay an absolute-band lookup (the current reading) or be judged relative to expectations: \"门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定\". Decided by Claude under that delegation: the definition below is Claude's analyst judgement, recorded as such, not Alex's words.\n  3052\t- Mechanism (arm 4 draw 1, all 356 judgements read, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md` §7 and `proof-judging-v6.txt`): 8 of 314 later judgements moved a rung and 320 of 356 reasons say \"remains\"; the FY2027 total revenue question was judged 12 times at neutral while its upward pushes grew from 1 to 35, every reason \"the $392 billion estimate is inside the band … does not establish $400 billion\"; the gross-margin judgement wrote \"leans toward rung 2 but does not warrant moving\"; the 2027 hyperscaler-capex theme stayed below the band management's own forecast names because the forecast \"is not fact\". The judging-v5 prompt asked the judge to \"be precise about what is established\" and said only fact can establish a rung: the model read \"established\" as the bar for leaving a rung and the consensus figure as the anchor. A second cause stays open: the ladder's neutral band is written at opening without naming what it compares against (PRD 06 ladder rule 2 asks for it); that is the extraction's rule and is not changed here.\n  3053\t- Decided, the analyst's rule: (1) the rung is a forecast, the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. (2) The reference is what the market expects: consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline; a consensus or guidance figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and, once other evidence has arrived, is never the reason to stay. (3) The judge derives the outcome the evidence implies (reported figures and guidance give a run-rate; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it), checks it against the dependencies' conclusions (a part cannot exceed its whole; a figure spanning several periods or products gives the question only its share), compares it with the rung boundaries and moves when it crosses one. (4) Weight follows tier and novelty: fact fixes what is known; party statements are the strongest forecast input; third-party views and rumours move the forecast in proportion to their specificity; a repeat, another outlet or an opinion with no new fact or calculation moves nothing. (5) The answer states `reference` and `implied_outcome` as required fields from `judging-v6` (`judging.schema_for`; code refuses an empty one; stored beside the rung in `judgements.reference` / `implied_outcome`; a ledger written before v6 gains the columns at its first write), so the D3 stance gold can read the reasoning, not only the rung. Written where the judgement is specified: PRD 06 State rules (`docs/system-design/new-facts.js` STATE_RULES, the generated block) and this record.\n  3054\t- Proof (`proof-judging-v6.txt`, `proof-judging-v6b.txt`: the last stored judgement request of 14 theses of arm 4 draw 1 re-sent once each under v6 and read beside the stored v5 answers, about a cent): every answer names the reference and derives the implied outcome. Six rungs moved against the stored ones: non-GAAP gross margin 3 → 2 (Q1 reported 75% and Q2 guided 75% sit on the rung-2 boundary), 2027 hyperscaler capex 4 → 5 (management's own \"more than $1 trillion\"), China accelerator share 4 → 5 (share \"fallen to zero\"), China H200 authorization No → Yes (a reported plan to permit named firms and reported progress in reviews, six months before the deadline), Data Center revenue 2 → 3 ($355–360 billion derived from Q1 and the total-revenue proxy, below the $360 billion boundary), Blackwell+Rubin revenue 2 → 1 in the first send by annualising a two-year \"$1 trillion visibility\" figure to $545 billion, a part above its whole: clause (3)'s consistency check was added for it and the re-send gives rung 2 ($320–360 billion, a share of the Data Center segment). Total revenue stays at 3 with the arithmetic shown (H1 $172.6 billion from Q1 and the Q2 guide; $400 billion needs more than $227 billion in H2). Prompt 2,453 → 3,782 characters: the request defined neither what a rung means nor a reference and its \"established\" wording forced the defect; the two sentences that carried it were cut. Configuration `poc-v90` (poc-v89 with judging-v6); the default stays `poc-v69`. Tests: `tests/test_stance_fields.py`. Measured by re-sent stored requests, not by an arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\").\n  3055\t\n  3056\t## D261 · 2026-11-02 · A ruler or gold that is built and reviewed is never changed again\n  3057\t\n  3058\t- Alex, 2026-11-02, while the judgement ruler (D3) was being built: \"你的尺子做出来和金标真的不能再动了，已经造成了3天的各种漂移，非常的严重，我需要你记录到我们的决策和原则里面，我们做完的review过的尺子金标不能再动了\".\n  3059\t- The drift he names, counted: the extraction ruler went from the first standard (D229, 2026-10-29) to the signed page version 3 (D243, the same day) to version 5 (D250, 2026-10-31), the gold was re-derived from version 3 to version 5 with 62 recorded changes, and every score between D248 and 2026-10-31 had been read against the version-3 gold (the \"假的测量\" of 2026-10-31); the judgement step had no ruler at all until today. Three days of numbers that cannot be compared with each other.\n  3060\t- Decided (his words; written at the decision it governs, AGENTS §7.1): once a ruler and its gold have been reviewed (readers who did not write them read them against the decisions; Alex signed), neither the definition nor the gold changes again. A defect found later is a dated correction record beside the gold (`corrections-*.json`), printed with every score and never merged in. A new definition is a new version that only his decision opens, with its own gold derived from scratch; old scores stay as they were and are never compared with the new. A ruler under construction is edited only until that review, and nothing is scored against it before.\n  3061\t- What is locked by this record: the extraction standard page (`docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html`, version 3 signed D243, with D250's four boundaries and counting unit) and `golden-v5/` (sha256 in `golden-v5.sha256`): no version 6; the loop's desk ruler (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/README.md`, D1–D3). What is still under construction and locks at his review: the judgement ruler `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/judgement-gold/ruler-v1.md`, its reader brief, question list and gold `gold-v1.json` (the sign-off is a separate record).\n  3062\t\n  3063\t## D262 · 2026-11-02 · The judgement ruler (D3) and its gold are fixed: the gold is reader B's answers; frozen at sha256 636c056d1e4252fa…\n  3064\t\n  3685\t## D354 · 2026-11-03 · Steps 3 and 4 (opening and matching questions, judging them) are frozen as `poc-v108` runs them, after three draws on the frozen extraction\n  3686\t\n  3687\t- Alex, after the extraction was frozen (D274): \"now that the extraction stage is done and frozen, we freeze that as well\"; on the plan to\n  3688\t  run the whole line on the frozen extraction and freeze steps 3 and 4 if their numbers did not get worse: \"好你跑\"; then \"那你跑了吧，我们赶紧确认step 3,4 可以freeze\".\n  3689\t- The run (`research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/log.md` row 29): `poc-v108` with the 22 frozen seeds over 2026-07-01..07-14, three draws at once\n  3690\t  from a pinned worktree, predictions and freeze conditions written before the send (`predictions-r9-frozen-v108.md`, sha256 beside it).\n  3691\t  All four conditions hold: every draw finished with no halted day; must-open questions 28/28 in every draw; the judgement agrees with the\n  3692\t  frozen gold on 15/17, 15/17 and 16/17 judged questions (control `poc-v94`: 16/18, 16/19, 16/18) and no question that agreed in all three\n  3693\t  control draws disagrees in all three new ones; core matters reaching judgement average 77.7 (control 74.3) and estimated noise reaching\n  3694\t  judgement 49.5 (bound 51).\n  3695\t- Frozen: the collision judge's prompt `collision-v2`, the judge's prompt `judging-v7`, the matching prompt the configuration names\n  6589\t## D543 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the cold reflection on the lean path: D518 stands with its reasons, the choice of system is not made in Alex's place, and no investigation is opened (reflection council consensus)\n  6590\t\n  6591\t- **The council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-2/`): Claude's own reflection written first\n  6592\t  (`own-reflection.md`); a fresh independent Codex session reading the whole record cold (`handoff-cold.md`, `cold-codex-1.md`);\n  6593\t  one challenge round (`cold-challenge-1.md`, `cold-codex-2.md`). Both readings, made apart, reached the same place.\n  6594\t- **Why the path did not reach its goal (agreed):** the fresh week mixed a difference of product policy with a comparison of\n  6595\t  quality (three of the old system's four covered matters are questions Alex's rule forbids the new system, D505); the evidence\n  6596\t  was too thin to rank answers (one run a system, seven answers against fifteen, readers' bars apart); the work followed each\n  6597\t  newly exposed defect instead of asking whether resolving it would select a system (the dependency stretch is the clearest\n  6598\t  case); and the council often corrected work already framed on a premise that the stored request, an earlier decision or the\n  6599\t  order of events contradicted.\n  6600\t- **Conclusions marked as weaker than they look:** \"no eligible judgement disagrees\" in the July comparison (few were eligible);\n  6601\t  \"36 of 438\" (repeated daily readings on a few question paths, not an error rate); the three unsupported answers with a\n  6602\t  missing stored figure (two matters, cause not shown); the new system's three confirmed missing pairs (a minimum; the one test\n  6603\t  was inconclusive); the dependency connection (a conditional replay; it also removes seven filing links).\n  6604\t- **Decided, citing D439:** D518 stands, restated with its reasons: the old system stays the default and both systems stay,\n  6605\t  for continuity and because the new system's answer-choice step has not passed its tests and it is not integrated with\n  6606\t  production storage. The quality of the two systems' answers is not ranked and **the choice of a foundation is not made in\n  6607\t  Alex's place** (the reviewer withdrew \"carry the old system forward provisionally\" as readable for such a choice). No\n  6608\t  investigation is opened: no bounded test on the record is likely to change the choice at a justified cost, and no narrow\n  6609\t  defect is reopened to postpone it. The two problems that do not depend on the choice stay recorded: related facts reaching\n  6610\t  the question that needs them (no common cause or tested general fix among the known cases), and the judge's amounts with\n  6611\t  nothing sizing them (what the product shows is Alex's choice). The pages were corrected where a cold reader could be misled\n  6612\t  (the advice's reasons; \"the one test that could decide\"; a stale \"waiting on Alex\" and an unsourced spend figure on the\n  6613\t  status page; \"three small mismatches\"; \"36 of 438\" without its qualification). A new step worth a decision returns to the\n  6614\t  council under D439.\n  9116\t## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\n  9117\t\n  9118\t- **Basis:**\n  9119\t  - Alex's \"你开始做\" on D653's next step and his D654 ruling (\"立通用规则\");\n  9120\t  - about $6 of testing authorized (\"你测试吧\"), of which about $4.34 is left.\n  9121\t- **The passage** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/edit.json`, version 5.5):\n  9122\t  - D654's three shapes and its share counter-case in D654's own words, two examples a shape from industries outside the 44;\n  9123\t  - one pointer to the same exception in the closing check, and one in the `no_ladder` description;\n  9124\t  - +1,528 characters across the three places, o200k system tokens 2,031 to 2,294, nothing cut (`cut_review`).\n  9125\t- **Audits:** fresh blind auditors of both families each round, v5.1 to v5.5. Both families read v5.5 SOUND (`audit-v55-codex.md`,\n  9126\t  `audit-v55-claude.md`). The inputs were frozen read-only per round from v5.4 on, after two Claude audits were voided by my replacing files mid-read.\n  9127\t- **The test** (`paired_probe.py`), astra on the frozen request against the edited one, interleaved:\n  9128\t  - targets acc/clean-8, acc/clean-9 and pool-17, 3 passes each;\n  9129\t  - u3/clean-10 (3 passes) and u2/clean-10 (2) are reported, not deciding. The scope rule: a case D654's words do not plainly name is reported. The\n  9130\t    two families split three times on u3/clean-10's easing form.\n  9131\t  - 5 decline controls and the share control u3/clean-11, 2 passes each;\n  9132\t  - 52 sends.\n  9133\t- **Verdict, fixed before the send:**\n  9134\t  - any lost edited answer gives FAIL;\n  9135\t  - fewer than 5 of 9 frozen target declines, or declines on fewer than 2 targets, gives INCONCLUSIVE;\n  9136\t  - PASS needs:\n  9137\t    - every edited target send written, with no hard-line fault from either family;\n  9138\t    - no material defect (wrong side, invented measure, second side dropped) from either source reviewer;\n  9139\t    - every edited control a decline neither family faults;\n  9140\t    - each share send does not ask the total;\n  9141\t  - due-day defects are reported, not deciding;\n  9142\t  - a stopped draw or a missed planted control gives NOT MEASURED.\n  9383\t## D664 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: no budget needed for the comparison; D658 waits; the council determines whether the six lines still make sense and what decides readiness\n  9384\t\n  9385\t- **Asked** (after D663):\n  9386\t  1. Should the six lines (D400) still block release, or be reported while readiness is decided by the product comparison, with \"beats\" set in\n  9387\t     numbers?\n  9388\t  2. May D658's new reference wait?\n  9389\t  3. The comparison's budget.\n  9390\t- **Alex:** \"3. no need for budget, 2. wait, 1. what are the rules, does it make sense now run your council to determine\".\n  9391\t- **Decided:**\n  9392\t  - The product comparison needs no budget set in advance. Each run still carries its own spend guard, and its price is reported. Provider caps\n  9393\t    are untouched.\n  9394\t  - D658 waits; design v8 is kept, and nothing is run.\n  9395\t  - Question 1 goes to a council, which determines it and records its consensus with his words, as an exercise of the authority he gave. The\n  9396\t    six lines were explained to him in plain words.\n  9397\t\n  9398\t## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n  9399\t\n  9400\t- **Council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/`):\n 10042\t## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n 10043\t\n 10044\t- **Context:** Alex's goal (D674) is to keep tackling until the comparison passes, without asking him. He has not answered the closing\n 10045\t  question. D544 says the council decides reversibly, not \"Alex's choice\".\n 10046\t- **Facts:**\n 10047\t  - A pass needs at least 9 of 14 rule-allowed matters only the new system serves, under D382; it serves 0–1 today.\n 10048\t  - The one-outcome probe failed its line 1.\n 10049\t  - The $0 census found three loss points that no wording fix reaches.\n 10050\t  - A verdict needs a full comparison, about $110, above D439's $40 ceiling.\n 10051\t  - Two decisions stand: D493 (no further Step 1 request change) and D505 (figures are not questions).\n 10052\t- **Council:** `docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/council-c-codex.md`: \"CONSENSUS: (a) Close the comparison loop, keep the old\n 10053\t  system running, and stop paid work … Reconsider if Alex reverses D505 or funds a full run. Before spending, show a path to passing the\n 10054\t  frozen criteria.\"\n 10055\t- **Decided:**\n 10056\t  - The loop is closed and the old system stays.\n 10057\t  - No paid work continues.\n 10058\t  - **Reversal conditions:** Alex reverses D505, or funds a full run. Either way, a written path to passing the frozen criteria comes\n 10059\t    first.\n 10060\t\n 10061\t## D678 · 2026-11-19 · Merge design (council consensus): the old system opens questions, the clean system reads and organises evidence, the same judge answers; a 12-article test awaits Alex's approval\nStart phase 2 with a $0 review of the 17 matters the old system never turned into questions.\n\n**Lessons.** The judge can make a mistake once and repeat it for days. For example, it added $25B and $18B without establishing whether they overlapped, then carried that reasoning forward. With identical full evidence, removing the prior answer changed the chosen range in 8 of 13 rejected cases. Keeping it changed zero. Test whether readers support the answer against same-day repeats, then replay from day one so each version builds its own history.\n\n**Weaker conclusions.** Only four of those eight moves earned both readers’ support, one short of the threshold. Two were the same capex question in different draws. M08 still failed, and removing the prior answer hurt the China-share answer on the frozen check. Changing output order and adding reasoning checks both failed their screens. H1’s new heading repaired zero of three cases selected to give it a chance. Moving the prior answer earlier remains untested. The fresh pool yielded only one eligible failure, so it could not test whether a fix generalizes.\n\n**Impact on the 32 matters.** Opening ranks first. Seventeen never opened, and M05, M09 and M25 were served in only one draw each. The unresolved company-figure policy could put five or six matters the old system serves out of reach. Judge reasoning cost M08 and M14. M30 is a possible gain if company figures remain eligible.\n\n**Next angle and falsifier.** Trace where each unopened matter first fell out and whether the evidence available then could support an answer. Count the attainable gains under each figure policy. If even the generous ceiling, including both possible judge repairs, is below five additional matters, change the plan to address the constraint that sets that ceiling. Otherwise, test the strongest opening fix on final answers, requiring five net gains and at least twice as many wins as losses.\n\nCONSENSUS-READY: Start the opening census and keep D198 in place while the census establishes what the hybrid can realistically gain.- The 4 net repairs without the previous conclusion are dev.\n- Gold 44.3 against 45.0 sits inside v7's own range of 44–46.\n- C100 is not yet rechecked.\n- The judge's attainable gain on the 32 matters is M08 and M14 at most, so +2 matters.\n\n**Remaining problems, by product impact (PLAN, \"Attainable\").**\n1. **Opening:** 17 of 32 matters are never opened, and 3 more are opened in only 1 of 3 draws. This is the release's gap.\n2. **D382** (company-figure questions): 5 to 6 matters, open with Alex.\n3. **The judge:** at most 2 matters, and only through a change to D198.\n\n**The next angle.**\n- Close the judge's anchor line within D198. Take D198's three options to Alex as a choice with a recommendation, not as a work order.\n- Start phase 2 now: the $0 census of why the 17 matters were never opened.\n- One cheap within-D198 lever remains untested: the previous conclusion placed before the evidence instead of last. Run it only if\n  the cold reader finds a mechanism that a label lacked. Otherwise it is another corner (D543).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
