ov 19 23:04 goldprobe-v7-noprev.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      462 Nov 19 22:40 goldprobe-v7.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     3028 Nov 19 22:52 hidden-flags.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@   8 lchingen  staff      256 Nov 20 01:09 ledger\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     6704 Nov 20 01:11 marks-diag.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff    26398 Nov 20 01:03 marks-fresh-census.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff    51135 Nov 19 23:16 marks-full.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   109643 Nov 19 23:16 marks-probe.json\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff   131894 Nov 20 01:15 opening-census.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 lchingen  staff      288 Nov 19 23:03 probe\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     3015 Nov 19 22:47 probe-J2a.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     2997 Nov 19 23:00 probe-J2b-noprev.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     3012 Nov 19 22:47 probe-J2b.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     1403 Nov 19 23:05 probe-v7-fullnoprev.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     1421 Nov 19 23:03 probe-v7-fullprev.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     2997 Nov 19 22:57 probe-v7-noprev.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     2996 Nov 19 22:40 probe-v7.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      918 Nov 19 23:16 probescore.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 lchingen  staff       96 Nov 19 22:43 prodpath\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      199 Nov 20 01:11 read-diag.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      288 Nov 20 00:57 read-fresh-census-2.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      288 Nov 20 00:59 read-fresh-census-3.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      539 Nov 20 01:03 read-fresh-census-4.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      526 Nov 20 00:54 read-fresh-census.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      624 Nov 19 23:16 read-full-2.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     1052 Nov 19 23:13 read-full.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff      543 Nov 19 23:16 read-probe-2.log\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff     1769 Nov 19 23:08 read-probe.log\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 lchingen  staff       96 Nov 19 22:54 window\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  staff    12284 Nov 19 22:55 window-old-2-replay.log\ntotal 368\ndrwxr-xr-x@  8 lchingen  staff     256 Nov 20 01:09 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 52 lchingen  staff    1664 Nov 20 01:15 ..\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff  157492 Nov 19 23:04 phase1.attempts.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff     180 Nov 19 23:04 phase1.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff       0 Nov 19 22:29 phase1.lock\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff   18303 Nov 20 01:09 phase1b.attempts.jsonl\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff     178 Nov 20 01:09 phase1b.json\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff       0 Nov 19 23:02 phase1b.lock\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:1:\"\"\"D260 (Alex, 2026-11-02: 门槛没有标准，按照你作为 hedge fund analyst 的认识来定): a judgement is a forecast against a reference.\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:2:The answer names the reference (what the market expects) and the implied outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies); the\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:17:ANSWER = {'rung': 2, 'reference': 'Consensus FY2027 revenue of $392 billion sits in rung 3.', 'implied_outcome': 'Q1 $81.6bn and Q2 guide $91bn give a run-rate above $400bn.',\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:22:def test_the_schema_requires_the_reference_and_the_implied_outcome():\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:25:    assert schema['required'][:3] == ['rung', 'reference', 'implied_outcome'] and schema['properties']['reference'] == {'type': 'string'}\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:27:    assert 'Judge against a reference' in system and 'implied_outcome' in system\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:36:def test_an_empty_reference_is_refused_and_both_fields_are_stored_beside_the_rung(tmp_path):\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:40:    assert judging.check_answer(conn, 'v1', dict(ANSWER, reference='  '), request_text) == [\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:41:        'reference is empty: state what the market expects and the figure or date the evidence implies']\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:42:    answer = types.SimpleNamespace(data=ANSWER, call_id=0, request_sha256='x', cached=False, cost_usd=0.0)\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:44:    row = conn.execute(\"select rung, reference, implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='v1'\").fetchone()\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:45:    assert (row['rung'], row['reference'], row['implied_outcome']) == (2, ANSWER['reference'], ANSWER['implied_outcome'])\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:48:def test_a_ledger_written_before_the_reference_fields_gains_the_stance_columns_when_opened_for_writing(tmp_path):\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:53:                   'request_sha256 text, publication_day text, theme_pushes_json text)')\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:57:    assert 'reference' in columns and 'implied_outcome' in columns\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:60:    older_answer = types.SimpleNamespace(data={k: v for k, v in ANSWER.items() if k not in judging.STANCE_FIELDS}, call_id=0, request_sha256='x', cached=False, cost_usd=0.0)\ntests/test_stance_fields.py:62:    assert tuple(reopened.execute(\"select reference, implied_outcome from judgements where view_id='v1'\").fetchone()) == (None, None)\ntests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:2:judging them, as `poc/config/poc-v108.json` runs them (its sha256 is pinned in test_frozen_extraction_prompt.py). Every piece that shapes\ntests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:23:def sha_of(value):\ntests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:24:    return hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(value, ensure_ascii=False, sort_keys=True).encode('utf-8')).hexdigest()\ntests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:30:            assert hashlib.sha256(handle.read()).hexdigest() == expected, f'{path} changed; steps 3 and 4 are frozen (D354)'\ntests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:34:    assert sha_of(judging.schema_for('judging-v7')) == JUDGING_SCHEMA_SHA\ntests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:36:    assert sha_of(questions) == MATCHER_QUESTIONS_SHA\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:12:A thesis records an investment question and its evidence. A date, ladder and other research details are conditional on the information available; missing details can be researched later. Evidence moves its state when it can be judged. Search then compare candidates with existing theses to merge, continue, create or skip; compare evidence within its thesis to repeat, replace or add. Extra source references alone do not trigger rejudgement. Extraction determines group associations; the writer preserves them after resolving final thesis IDs under the [grouping contract](#research-groups-associate-during-extraction).\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:19:- The model judges from the evidence in view (the arrivals since its fifth most recent judgement and the basis its last ten judgements cited; the rest stays in force, D198) and dependency conclusions, rather than adjusting its previous score. A revision follows statement date, so a late older statement is stored as one more piece and never recorded as revising a newer one (D202).\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:37:│       ├─ State → The thesis's current ladder rung (Evidence pushes towards either end; the model forecasts the rung most likely at the due date, against a reference (D260). A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it.)\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:89:| State | Our judgement of the thesis's current rung; evidence pushes toward either end | The model judges the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, against a reference (below). It reads the evidence in view, the arrivals since its fifth most recent judgement and the basis its last ten judgements cited, the request naming how many more pieces stay in force (D198); a revision is shown beside the piece it revises and a repeat beside the piece the matcher read it as, both in force (D202, D204); plus current dependency states and reasons and, for an asset thesis, the theme block. Do not increment or decrement the previous score. Cite evidence and compare with the conclusion before this round to state whether it changed. Do not rejudge if only source references were added and dependency conclusions did not change. | After the 8-K: strongly bearish |\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:91:- Every judgement states its basis in a fixed response shape: evidence IDs such as e12 and e15, plus dependency thesis IDs such as #1 when their changes triggered rejudgement.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:92:- Code checks cited IDs against the request that was sent: evidence must be among the pieces shown to this thesis (D198); cited theses must be its dependencies. Accept only if all checks pass. Otherwise record the reason and ask for one corrected judgement. If that also fails, use normal failure handling: retry from this step, then human review after repeated failure. This checks references, not whether the judgement is correct, like verifying a cited page exists.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:95:- The rung is a forecast against a reference (D260): the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, judged against what the market expects (consensus, guidance, the stated plan or deadline). The judgement names the reference and its rung and the outcome the evidence implies (a figure or date derived from reported figures, guidance and quantified revisions), and moves when the implied outcome crosses a rung boundary. A consensus figure alone keeps the judgement at the reference's rung and is not the reason to stay once other evidence has arrived; \"not established\" is confidence, not a reason to stay. From judging-v6 the reference and the implied outcome are required fields of the answer, stored beside the rung; an empty one is refused.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:133:- Rejudge an open thesis when its inputs change: new evidence, replacement, a new link to existing evidence, a dependency declaring a changed conclusion, or (for an asset thesis) a theme thesis declaring one. Additional source references alone do not count. Binding an awaited A or moving to its successor also changes B's inputs. Closed theses do not update. A memo-derived thesis is first judged when evidence first links to it; before that, it and its dependants see “not yet judged”.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:148:<!-- generated: shape -->\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:156:<!-- /generated: shape -->\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:166:  ↓ 2 Receive evidence (Code): Retries do not duplicate evidence. A revised input updates only its own source reference. A revised retelling does not alter the original evidence. If the revision is from the original source, compare its statements normally: a changed statement is stored as a revision of the old one, both in force (D202).\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:169:  ↓ 5 Validate (Code): Destination IDs must be in the shown lists or the relevant thesis's evidence. Merge only into open theses. New subjects must resolve within the universe using classification's identifier rules; otherwise skip. Dependencies must reference shown theses or an explicit awaited chain/year and remain acyclic. Return invalid answers for correction.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:171:  ↓ 7 Run the day's rejudgement round (Model): Once a day, after the day's last item (D63), rejudge only open theses whose inputs changed that day: new or newly linked evidence (a repeat or a revision is a new piece), or a changed dependency conclusion, newly created awaited thesis or successor. Judge dependencies first, then theme theses before asset theses, and each thesis once per round; each judgement reads the evidence in view (D198). Extra source references alone do not trigger it. Memo-derived theses without evidence stay not yet judged. Each judgement declares whether its conclusion changed; changed conclusions propagate to dependants, and a theme's to every open asset thesis (D195). The round's queue is read from the ledger, so a resumed round recovers what an earlier commit queued.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:185:- The D155 POC uses code for fully determined duplicate identity and model comparison when scope or legacy identity needs judgement. A shared quantity (an aggregate opened under its admission reason) is one thesis per theme, measure and period: its population or wording is not identity, so code merges another wording into the open one and succeeds it for the next period (D197). Reference lists guide research without vetoing candidates. Same group does not mean same thesis. See docs/poc/grouping-improvement-plan.md for the contract and measured scope.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:186:- Search finds plausible candidates; the model handles semantic comparison. H20 and Blackwell export licences can look similar but are separate questions. Bullish and bearish accounts of one question share its identity.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:306:| Source | Upstream ID, category, publication day and location. A number repeated in text and tables within one item adds references to the same piece; a retelling or repeated statement in another item is its own piece, with the pair recorded as the same claim (D204). |\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:319:- Order by sequence, never the computer clock. Before each item, extraction reads the latest committed questions from earlier sequences, including earlier same-day writes (D375). The two experimental split calls share that snapshot. Processing must be equivalent to sequence order: if an earlier item changes the snapshot, including by opening a question, redo any later work that used the stale snapshot.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:323:- A revised input changes only its own source reference. Revising a retelling does not change original evidence. For an original-source revision, a changed statement is stored as a revision of the old one, both in force; nothing is retired (D202). Rejudge each open thesis linked to affected statements once. A retelling-reference change alone does not trigger rejudgement. Keep old judgement records unchanged.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:334:| Extraction | Receive sourced evidence and candidates. Before each item, supply the item's subjects' open questions and all open theme questions with takes lines, as committed before the item; both experimental split calls share that snapshot (D375). No states, evidence, dependency links or list of stored groups. |\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:346:- Every comparison records shown input, raw response, Config version and decision maker. Reject destinations outside the shown lists or relevant evidence, and dependencies not shown or explicitly awaiting a chain/year, including cycles.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:349:- Rejudge only open theses with changed inputs: new or newly linked evidence (repeats and revisions are new pieces), or changed dependency conclusions. Memo-derived theses without evidence remain unjudged. Cite evidence and relevant dependency IDs, and declare conclusion change. First judgement and rung changes must declare a change. The rung is a forecast of the most likely outcome at the due date, against a reference (D260).\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:353:- Append knowledge in arrival order. Store a late older statement as one more piece with its true date and no revision (D202); accept newly learned matters with their true dates. A revised retelling changes only its own source reference. An original-source revision's changed statements are stored as revisions, both in force; nothing is retired (D202).\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:380:- D47: consistent terms, evidence comparison after candidate resolution, dependency references in judgement reasons and Reuters example correction.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:395:- D149 requirement: organise theses by the continuing business process they discuss, called a research group. Vera Rubin readiness and customer deployment can share a group while shipment dates, SK factory launch and OpenAI deployment retain separate questions, ladders and due dates. A group may start with one thesis; a thesis may belong to several groups. A group has no state or ladder, creates no automatic dependency and is not an overarching investment thesis for an agent.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:396:- Associate by business process, across companies and industries, not merely by company. A customer deployment explicitly using Rubin can join Rubin; NVIDIA PC chips cannot join just because they share a company. OpenAI deployment cannot join an SK-specific group merely because both involve Rubin. A group does not replace a research-universe theme.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:397:- The full-text call shows no list of stored groups; an open thesis's takes line names the groups it belongs to (D264). During that call, extraction declares named and scoped groups. A candidate that tracks an ongoing matter (a product rollout and its deployments, a deal, a policy process, an investment or demand cycle) cites one or more groups it declared, without repeats; a company's own reported or guided financial lines (total or segment revenue, margins, expenses, tax rate, capex) belong to the company and cite none unless the line itself tracks such a matter (D165). Code validates the references before writing, folds a declared group into a stored one by its names (D166, D257), and creates a declared group only when a written thesis that tracks a matter cites it, so a company's lines alone never found a group.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:402:- Historical implementation reference: D147's isolated grouping prototype and its field names are preserved in the research records. D165 and D169 subsequently integrated grouping into the default pipeline. See docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md for the current implementation and measured limits; the old prototype does not establish large-library recall.\n446:- **Next:** superseded by D681, below.\n448:**The one next task: Alex's answer on the hybrid's release line (D681–D688, 2026-11-20).** Alex opened the hybrid's build and\n449:test, and asked that problems not be found only at the end (his words are in the D681 record). Plan: [PLAN.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md). Design:\n464:  - **The judge line is paused within D198.** Four angles have failed:\n468:  - The carried derivation holds the rejected rungs. Every remaining lever changes D198.\n477:- **Attainable check (D688, council M):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md), last two sections.\n481:  - What binds: the list counts finer than D248/D388 on 9 matters, the NVIDIA-only subject on 5, and D198 on 2.\n483:- **Waiting on Alex (D688):**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4871,4880p;6595,6614p;8908,8925p;9080,9162p;9383,9403p;10042,10061p;10079,10110p;10162,10174p'; cat poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/ledger/phase1.json poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/ledger/phase1b.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '4871,4880p;6595,6614p;8908,8925p;9080,9162p;9383,9403p;10042,10061p;10079,10110p;10162,10174p'; cat poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/ledger/phase1.json poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/ledger/phase1b.json\"","aggregated_output":"  4871\t## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n  4872\t\n  4873\t- **Alex, 2026-11-13** (unprompted, after a recap of the goal): \"把这个goal 改成更多的要求council in the loop 来自行的根据数据和目标做决策。我接下来不会active,需要你有问题的时候就fire council 然后和claude 掰扯直到你们能达到共识为止再下去执行，并仔细的测量，自己看trace 然后把每一轮log 做学习总结，不要饭一样的错，词学迭代完成我们的PRD生产目标\".\n  4874\t- **Decided (his words):** while he is not active, every choice or next step that would have gone to him goes to the council: an independent read-only Codex review and Claude argue it on the data, the PRD and its quantified goals until they reach a consensus; the consensus is recorded as a decision citing D439, executed, measured, every trace read by Claude itself, and every round logged with a learning summary so the same mistake is not made twice; the loop iterates until the PRD's production goals are met.\n  4875\t- **Settled by Claude (wording and limits, not confirmed by Alex):** the standing limits of AGENTS.md stay (the frozen ruler never changes; nothing pushed, deployed, published or committed unasked; credentials and provider caps untouched). Opening a new version of a piece frozen for \"a new version only Alex opens\" is a council decision under D439; the frozen ruler is not. A disagreement the council cannot settle is recorded with both positions and the cheaper, reversible course is taken. **Spending ceiling:** paid model calls in this period stay within $40 at published rates in total, each paid step with its own ceiling in its council-agreed design; this figure is Claude's setting, not Alex's, and is reported in every status update.\n  4876\t- **Where written:** AGENTS.md, \"Authority and scope\" (the D439 bullet) and §7.3 \"Own the loop\"; `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`; the memory file `feedback-council-decides-while-alex-away.md`. The session goal itself is set by Alex's `/goal` command; the replacement text is given to him in the reply.\n  4877\t- **Scope:** all modules Alex has taken up; the current work is clean Step 1 (gates 2 and 3 of `clean-arch/step1-diagnosis-2026-11-12/COMBINED-PLAN.md`), then the Step 4 judgement faults that kept Stage B from passing.\n  4878\t\n  4879\t## D440 · 2026-11-13 · Gate 2 failed; a memory diagnostic decides whether c15yc goes on (council consensus under D439)\n  4880\t\n  6595\t  quality (three of the old system's four covered matters are questions Alex's rule forbids the new system, D505); the evidence\n  6596\t  was too thin to rank answers (one run a system, seven answers against fifteen, readers' bars apart); the work followed each\n  6597\t  newly exposed defect instead of asking whether resolving it would select a system (the dependency stretch is the clearest\n  6598\t  case); and the council often corrected work already framed on a premise that the stored request, an earlier decision or the\n  6599\t  order of events contradicted.\n  6600\t- **Conclusions marked as weaker than they look:** \"no eligible judgement disagrees\" in the July comparison (few were eligible);\n  6601\t  \"36 of 438\" (repeated daily readings on a few question paths, not an error rate); the three unsupported answers with a\n  6602\t  missing stored figure (two matters, cause not shown); the new system's three confirmed missing pairs (a minimum; the one test\n  6603\t  was inconclusive); the dependency connection (a conditional replay; it also removes seven filing links).\n  6604\t- **Decided, citing D439:** D518 stands, restated with its reasons: the old system stays the default and both systems stay,\n  6605\t  for continuity and because the new system's answer-choice step has not passed its tests and it is not integrated with\n  6606\t  production storage. The quality of the two systems' answers is not ranked and **the choice of a foundation is not made in\n  6607\t  Alex's place** (the reviewer withdrew \"carry the old system forward provisionally\" as readable for such a choice). No\n  6608\t  investigation is opened: no bounded test on the record is likely to change the choice at a justified cost, and no narrow\n  6609\t  defect is reopened to postpone it. The two problems that do not depend on the choice stay recorded: related facts reaching\n  6610\t  the question that needs them (no common cause or tested general fix among the known cases), and the judge's amounts with\n  6611\t  nothing sizing them (what the product shows is Alex's choice). The pages were corrected where a cold reader could be misled\n  6612\t  (the advice's reasons; \"the one test that could decide\"; a stale \"waiting on Alex\" and an unsourced spend figure on the\n  6613\t  status page; \"three small mismatches\"; \"36 of 438\" without its qualification). A new step worth a decision returns to the\n  6614\t  council under D439.\n  8908\t- **Cost:** Opus is about $0.058 a topic, about 65 times luna and not below astra. It counts about 68% more input tokens. The pre-send\n  8909\t  estimate was wrong.\n  8910\t- **Not established:** whether Opus is better. One family sees a tie, and Claude-family leniency toward Claude's writing is not\n  8911\t  excluded.\n  8912\t- **Spending:** D439 stands at about $39.29 of $40, including run-1's $0.026.\n  8913\t\n  8914\t## D648 · 2026-11-17 · Alex reverses D645: the answer-choice step uses astra; gate 1 on the 44 is launched with astra-frozen\n  8915\t\n  8916\t- **Alex, 2026-11-17**, on the Opus result and the proposal to test Haiku 5.5: \"不要。那就用astra 吧。你之前的实验可以跑，但你真的确定这个不会是一个很大的烧钱窟窿吗？我之后未来可能有1000个资产类别许啊哟process\".\n  8917\t- **Decided (his words):**\n  8918\t  - astra is the candidate model for the answer-choice step, which reverses D645;\n  8919\t  - Haiku 5.5 is not tested;\n  8920\t  - the prepared gate-1 experiment runs, which lifts D426's \"no fifth Stage A\" for this run.\n  8921\t- **Settled by Claude, and recorded as such:**\n  8922\t  - **The configuration is `astra-frozen`.** It is the only one measured: 4 of 78 failed sends outside the 44 (D633, D634).\n  8923\t    `astra-a2-v2` has never been measured as a pair.\n  8924\t  - **The cap is $9.50,** the README's figure: expected $4.88 to $6.60, plus two attempts in flight at $1.21. The cap is\n  8925\t    `gate1-candidate/authorization.json`, which quotes his words.\n  9080\t    - one bet seen from two sides, where the relation holds;\n  9081\t    - the outcome stays the source of what is tracked (D397);\n  9082\t    - no description-first priority (D631, D635);\n  9083\t    - examples from other industries, none from the 44;\n  9084\t    - a blind whole-request reader, with D631's six cases left undecided.\n  9085\t\n  9086\t    If the distinction cannot be written without an unsupported priority, it stops.\n  9087\t  - **Then,** only on a pass, a paired exposed verification: unchanged against edited astra, 4 targets × 3 passes and 8 controls × 2 passes each arm, a\n  9088\t    strict no-new-fault rule, about $2.1.\n  9089\t  - **Then,** a separate decision on the exposed gate-1 run, whose budget goes to Alex.\n  9090\t- **For Alex:** D592's gate-2 reference, and the cost comparison.\n  9091\t- **Spending:** $1.66 of the ~$6 he authorized for testing on 2026-11-17.\n  9092\t\n  9093\t## D654 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: a general rule for the answer-choice step — a total with its share, a volume with its shortage, demand with capacity keeping pace: ask the total, the volume or the demand\n  9094\t\n  9095\t- **Asked** (deep council round 5's wording):\n  9096\t  - \"写题那一步，遇到'结果'里同时写着两样、又没说哪个是主的话题，要不要立一条通用规则？\" It named the three shapes with examples: a total and one kind's share\n  9097\t    of it (world chip revenue and its AI-chip part); shipments and whether supply stays short (HBM); demand and whether capacity keeps pace.\n  9098\t  - The facts given: astra declines all of them as \"分不出主次\", and they are all 7 of its gate-1 misses. His own D436 words covered only the HBM\n  9099\t    shipments-and-shortage pair; the other two orientations are the record's.\n  9100\t  - The cost given: a topic that really tracks the share could be asked as the total; mitigated by \"题目追的就是份额本身时，就问份额\".\n  9101\t  - **Options:**\n  9102\t    - the general rule (recommended);\n  9103\t    - only the theses he ruled on;\n  9104\t    - no rule.\n  9105\t- **Alex:** \"立通用规则 (Recommended)\".\n  9106\t- **Decided:** for the three shapes, when the outcome tracks a figure and also names one of these second sides of the same bet, the figure is the question\n  9107\t  and the second side is listed as not judged. These are not \"several things with none the main one\". When the outcome tracks the share itself, with the\n  9108\t  total only as its base, the share is the question.\n  9109\t  - This settles the scope question four Codex-family auditors raised (D653 rounds 3 to 5).\n  9110\t- **Next:**\n  9111\t  - an independent audit of the exact passage (narrow-d436 v5.1) against this ruling and the request;\n  9112\t  - the paired exposed verification, tightened per council round 5: a material defect marked by either reviewer blocks a pass; u3/clean-11 checks only\n  9113\t    that the total is not asked; u2/clean-10 is reported, not deciding; the scoring and spending paths are exercised at $0 before the send.\n  9114\t- **Scope:** the clean path's ladder step (Step 4a); the frozen request is unchanged until a measured version is adopted.\n  9115\t\n  9116\t## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\n  9117\t\n  9118\t- **Basis:**\n  9119\t  - Alex's \"你开始做\" on D653's next step and his D654 ruling (\"立通用规则\");\n  9120\t  - about $6 of testing authorized (\"你测试吧\"), of which about $4.34 is left.\n  9121\t- **The passage** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-8/narrow-d436/edit.json`, version 5.5):\n  9122\t  - D654's three shapes and its share counter-case in D654's own words, two examples a shape from industries outside the 44;\n  9123\t  - one pointer to the same exception in the closing check, and one in the `no_ladder` description;\n  9124\t  - +1,528 characters across the three places, o200k system tokens 2,031 to 2,294, nothing cut (`cut_review`).\n  9125\t- **Audits:** fresh blind auditors of both families each round, v5.1 to v5.5. Both families read v5.5 SOUND (`audit-v55-codex.md`,\n  9126\t  `audit-v55-claude.md`). The inputs were frozen read-only per round from v5.4 on, after two Claude audits were voided by my replacing files mid-read.\n  9127\t- **The test** (`paired_probe.py`), astra on the frozen request against the edited one, interleaved:\n  9128\t  - targets acc/clean-8, acc/clean-9 and pool-17, 3 passes each;\n  9129\t  - u3/clean-10 (3 passes) and u2/clean-10 (2) are reported, not deciding. The scope rule: a case D654's words do not plainly name is reported. The\n  9130\t    two families split three times on u3/clean-10's easing form.\n  9131\t  - 5 decline controls and the share control u3/clean-11, 2 passes each;\n  9132\t  - 52 sends.\n  9133\t- **Verdict, fixed before the send:**\n  9134\t  - any lost edited answer gives FAIL;\n  9135\t  - fewer than 5 of 9 frozen target declines, or declines on fewer than 2 targets, gives INCONCLUSIVE;\n  9136\t  - PASS needs:\n  9137\t    - every edited target send written, with no hard-line fault from either family;\n  9138\t    - no material defect (wrong side, invented measure, second side dropped) from either source reviewer;\n  9139\t    - every edited control a decline neither family faults;\n  9140\t    - each share send does not ask the total;\n  9141\t  - due-day defects are reported, not deciding;\n  9142\t  - a stopped draw or a missed planted control gives NOT MEASURED.\n  9143\t- **Code:** 17 tests at $0 (the verdict paths, and a dry run of all six draws and the reading with stored astra answers). No mutant was run: the\n  9144\t  machine's guard refused scratch mirrors earlier.\n  9145\t- **Council:** rounds 4 to 6c on thread 01a1e8ee-437f-74a3-ad0a-8edcbde0e3b3.\n  9146\t  - Round 5 disagreed and sent the scope question to Alex (D654).\n  9147\t  - Round 6 corrected two verdict rules and the budget wording.\n  9148\t  - Round 6b corrected the verdict order.\n  9149\t  - Round 6c: \"CONSENSUS: send the paired test under the shared $3.60 cap … a pass is evidence on this exposed test, not a Gate 1 pass or proof of\n  9150\t    general performance.\"\n  9151\t- **Cost:** estimated about $2.15 with the system text cached and about $3.2 uncached. These come from stored mean tokens and are not bounds.\n  9152\t- **Next:**\n  9153\t  - the reading by both families with the planted controls, and two source reviewers;\n  9154\t  - third readers on disputes, with the prewritten strict counting kept in the verdict;\n  9155\t  - every trace read by Claude;\n  9156\t  - a decision recording the result.\n  9157\t\n  9158\t## D656 · 2026-11-17 · The paired test of v5.5 (D655): FAIL by the prewritten rule; D654's class recovered on the exposed targets; v5.5 kept as an unaccepted candidate; next, a $0 census of the listing defect\n  9159\t\n  9160\t- **Run:** `poc/data/clean-narrow-d436-paired-2026-11-17/run-1`. 52 sends, none lost; spent $1.52 against a cap of $3.60. The score is in\n  9161\t  `score-output.txt` and the keys in `keys/`.\n  9162\t- **Reading:**\n  9383\t## D664 · 2026-11-17 · Alex: no budget needed for the comparison; D658 waits; the council determines whether the six lines still make sense and what decides readiness\n  9384\t\n  9385\t- **Asked** (after D663):\n  9386\t  1. Should the six lines (D400) still block release, or be reported while readiness is decided by the product comparison, with \"beats\" set in\n  9387\t     numbers?\n  9388\t  2. May D658's new reference wait?\n  9389\t  3. The comparison's budget.\n  9390\t- **Alex:** \"3. no need for budget, 2. wait, 1. what are the rules, does it make sense now run your council to determine\".\n  9391\t- **Decided:**\n  9392\t  - The product comparison needs no budget set in advance. Each run still carries its own spend guard, and its price is reported. Provider caps\n  9393\t    are untouched.\n  9394\t  - D658 waits; design v8 is kept, and nothing is run.\n  9395\t  - Question 1 goes to a council, which determines it and records its consensus with his words, as an exercise of the authority he gave. The\n  9396\t    six lines were explained to him in plain words.\n  9397\t\n  9398\t## D665 · 2026-11-17 · Council (D664, Alex's \"run your council to determine\"): the six lines stop blocking release; one product comparison against the running pipeline decides readiness, its verdict written before the first send (council consensus)\n  9399\t\n  9400\t- **Council** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/reflection-10/`):\n  9401\t  - Claude's own position, written first (`own-position.md`);\n  9402\t  - the Codex reading (`codex-1.md`, thread 01a1ebfe-4f67-7c72-af87-7830055e0f09, memories off);\n  9403\t  - the Claude-family reading (`claude-1.md`);\n 10042\t## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n 10043\t\n 10044\t- **Context:** Alex's goal (D674) is to keep tackling until the comparison passes, without asking him. He has not answered the closing\n 10045\t  question. D544 says the council decides reversibly, not \"Alex's choice\".\n 10046\t- **Facts:**\n 10047\t  - A pass needs at least 9 of 14 rule-allowed matters only the new system serves, under D382; it serves 0–1 today.\n 10048\t  - The one-outcome probe failed its line 1.\n 10049\t  - The $0 census found three loss points that no wording fix reaches.\n 10050\t  - A verdict needs a full comparison, about $110, above D439's $40 ceiling.\n 10051\t  - Two decisions stand: D493 (no further Step 1 request change) and D505 (figures are not questions).\n 10052\t- **Council:** `docs/research/2026-11-19-comparison-review/council-c-codex.md`: \"CONSENSUS: (a) Close the comparison loop, keep the old\n 10053\t  system running, and stop paid work … Reconsider if Alex reverses D505 or funds a full run. Before spending, show a path to passing the\n 10054\t  frozen criteria.\"\n 10055\t- **Decided:**\n 10056\t  - The loop is closed and the old system stays.\n 10057\t  - No paid work continues.\n 10058\t  - **Reversal conditions:** Alex reverses D505, or funds a full run. Either way, a written path to passing the frozen criteria comes\n 10059\t    first.\n 10060\t\n 10061\t## D678 · 2026-11-19 · Merge design (council consensus): the old system opens questions, the clean system reads and organises evidence, the same judge answers; a 12-article test awaits Alex's approval\n 10079\t## D679 · 2026-11-19 · Alex lifts D677's paid-send stop for the merge test only; the test runs on 70 articles, two old draws, two judging arms, under a $5 ledger\n 10080\t\n 10081\t- **Alex (the session goal):** \"write the plan, execute the plan, and don't do full blown runs, validate it works based on metrics we\n 10082\t  meassure for quality\".\n 10083\t- **The plan:** `docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/EXECUTION-PLAN.md`, revised by council rounds c and d (`council-c-codex.md`,\n 10084\t  `council-d-codex.md`).\n 10085\t- **The article set.** It became the 70 window articles that either system tied to M04 and M17, plus the census and the control.\n 10086\t  - My first count read the census numbers as positions in `kept-articles.json`. They are numbers in `census/numbering.json`. Codex\n 10087\t    caught it.\n 10088\t  - The same misreading put custom-chip and DRAM theses into a first list of 126.\n 10089\t- **Per-article open lists** were agreed in round d: the old questions open when the article was read.\n 10090\t- **The judging copy.** A 09-06 cutoff copy of each old store, with the frozen judge restricted to the target questions on one daily\n 10091\t  schedule for both arms (hybrid: c8's filing; control: old's own evidence).\n 10092\t- **Checks before any send ($0):**\n 10093\t  - c8's request, rebuilt, equals the stored c8 request byte for byte.\n 10094\t  - The control arm, answered with old's archived answers on old's schedule, rebuilt 25 of 25 capex requests byte for byte, and all 22\n 10095\t    Anthropic requests with the same evidence. Their only difference is the theme block: other questions held at 09-06.\n 10096\t- **Lines** P1, P2, P3 and P5 hold in both draws, plus a validity line V; P4 is diagnostic only.\n 10097\t- **Ceiling:** $5 on a new ledger. The estimate is about $1.4 for c8 and about $0.2 for judging. This is within D439's $40.\n 10098\t- **Also recorded:** PATH-TO-PASS's census C named new-2's clean-26 and clean-7, and new-3's clean-29, clean-6 and clean-12, as capex\n 10099\t  theses. They are custom-chip and memory theses, so census C's capex reading is to be re-checked before it is relied on.\n 10100\t\n 10101\t\n 10102\t## D680 · 2026-11-19 · Merge test closed (council e): delivery verified, the registered test did not pass (P2's proxy clause and V missed)\n 10103\t\n 10104\t- **Ran under D679**, for $2.13 of a $5 ledger: 140 c8 sends, 98 judge calls in two arms, 15 noise re-sends, and two blind reader\n 10105\t  families on 20 cards with 5 controls.\n 10106\t- **Held:**\n 10107\t  - P1, delivery, 4/4: the hybrid's final requests carry c8's four-company $720–745B item and the Reuters anchor-talks items;\n 10108\t  - P3, talks stay talks, 2/2;\n 10109\t  - P5, both readers support all 4 hybrid answers, settled in round 0;\n 10110\t  - P4 (diagnostic): 0 NVIDIA-figure proposals of 7;\n 10162\t  - Sent without it: v7 moves 14 of 24 targets (2 with it) and 2 of 24 controls, mostly toward the rung the readers named. J2b without\n 10163\t    it moves 16.\n 10164\t  - It is confounded: in 34 of 48 requests, the previous conclusion also carries hidden pieces (D198).\n 10165\t- **Decided (council):**\n 10166\t  - retire J2a and J2b;\n 10167\t  - separate the anchor from the hidden pieces on complete evidence: 21 cases with 1 to 100 hidden pieces, every piece in force shown\n 10168\t    (each request first rebuilt byte for byte by `build_prompt` on the store as it stood, 48/48), with and without the previous\n 10169\t    conclusion, and a screen written before the send;\n 10170\t  - the end-to-end test of a judge change is a judge-only replay of the whole window from 07-01 with old's links fixed. It is validated\n 10171\t    at $0: 82/82 days with the same judged set, and 1,612 of 1,616 requests byte-identical (the 4 others are retries);\n 10172\t  - a new $2 ledger for the separating test, inside D439's $40.\n 10173\t- **For Alex after the separation:** whether to change how the previous conclusion is presented (within D198), or what it carries\n 10174\t  (a change to D198).\n{\n \"ceiling\": 3.0,\n \"spent\": 2.6413292399999997,\n \"reserved\": 1.0755285551056204e-16,\n \"overrun\": false,\n \"refused\": 0,\n \"attempts\": 1356,\n \"stopped\": false,\n \"stop_reason\": null\n}{\n \"ceiling\": 2.0,\n \"spent\": 0.3574589199999999,\n \"reserved\": 3.469446951953614e-17,\n \"overrun\": false,\n \"refused\": 0,\n \"attempts\": 156,\n \"stopped\": false,\n \"stop_reason\": null\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '185,201p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 8 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md; sed -n '448,487p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; rg -n 'judging|phase1|conclusion' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '185,201p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 8 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md; sed -n '448,487p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; rg -n 'judging|phase1|conclusion' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-brief.md\"","aggregated_output":"| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n\n- \"你这个单独开一个专题出来解决 … 是promot，是系统结构设计还是到底哪里有问题挂错一堆东西，机制是不是有问题（一定要挂吗？有没有可能是杂音\" (2026-11-03)\n- \"So if it's a customer problem or other companies that you think is relating NVIDIA and it's the wrong evidence, then what is the standard for it? … from a hedge fund analyst standpoint, are these even relevant? Do you think your ruler is wrong in this aspect?\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你确定下你接下来要改进的量化目标，以及你要看到端到端我们的管线是要做什么的，不要乱硬优化，要看到目标\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"就测试一种，一次 … 能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"这些只是类型题，你需要抽象拔高我们现在的核心问题和卡点。这个很重要这样改下去才是对的\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\" (2026-11-04)\n- \"go\" (2026-11-04, on the proposed amendments to §5.2 and §6 and on this test)\n| 34 | 11-05 | 第三版的登记测试：和第 8 轮一样，只换这一句；读 132 次（0.078 美元）、两人分类（第二位盲分）、读到数的 7 道题三遍重判、当天对照（108 次，0.268 美元） | **三条全过**：v10、v12 各 9/9；判对的题一道没变错（只有 v22 第 2 遍反过来对照 0/3、起点组 3/3，理由是在 41% 和 32% 两个增长估计间摇摆，和第 13 轮方向相反，与起点数无关）；46 个数全是自己的量（2 条是标明的二季度指引），两人分类全一致；v19、v20 的错数全没了，其余 15 道白卷、没冒出新错。没盖住：资本开支那一行试发时漏过 1 次；指引也被写成\"事实\"；一路判下来的效果和跨题效果要端到端才量得到 | 交 Alex：要不要做进生产、跑 14 天三遍端到端 |\n| 35 | 11-05 | 独立读者挑战\"现在做进生产、跑 14 天三遍\"的建议 | 核实属实的：资本开支那一行在新句子下 12 次读漏 3 次（旧句子 9/9，模型两次都怪\"更大的行\"半句）；句子照 5 月财报改、又只在 5 月财报上量，没有留出的财报；做进生产前的记录写法（同一个数挂几道题、指引不该写成\"事实\"、第二个提示词）要 Alex 定；分类和判断同时跑、说明里还引着旧句子，照实记下 | 建议撤回；下一步：修掉资本开支漏读（改成\"写完逐条复核\"），在 5 月和留出的 8 月两份财报上各测一遍，约 0.5 美元 |\n| 36 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好开始做到production 上，完整的更新所有系统设计等\"；同一个数挂几道题，他选\"存一条，挂到每道读到它的题\"（D364）。做进生产前先修资本开支漏读：第四版把\"是不是这道题的量\"挪到最后逐条复核（并删掉别的期间），文件规则补\"有申报的只读申报的\"；Codex 审 3 轮（共 6 条严重，都改）；试发 7 道题过；然后 5 月登记读法、8 月留出读法 | **没过**：5 月\"不能删掉该留的\"——v22 只留住 1/3、资本开支 3/6 读；8 月资本开支二季度 0/3（选了上半年、引用跳格被拒）。机理：复核里\"别的期间删掉\"让全年题删掉最近一季；\"最近一期\"在本季和年初至今两栏间没说清。好消息：8 月 v9 找到了新披露的担保 1,085 亿和承诺 560 亿 | 停，交 Alex：第三版是唯一过了 5 月三条的版本 |\n| 37 | 11-05 | Alex：\"为什么没过？…你确定是正确的rejection 吗？你又下去看trace吗？\"；\"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信下一步你要跑什么才能收敛\"。普查全部 7 次读法、606 次文件读（`census_all_reads.py`，$0） | 第三版 0 个错数、156 次读漏 3 次（全是资本开支）；第二版 2 个错数；第四版漏 24 次（5 月）、16 次（8 月）。我自己判错的：6 个对的数被我的引用检查拒（漏星号、跳格），8 月\"只认本季\"规则错，第 13 轮 3 条\"有争议\"的数是标准答案自己用的行，第三版全过后又改第四版 | 收敛方案：提示词定为第三版不再改；修引用检查（$0 重放全部 606 次读核对）；在 8 月财报上用第三版读一次（约 8 美分，只有\"收错数\"能叫停）；然后做进生产 |\n| 38 | 11-05 | Alex：\"好，按这三步做，你不要再搬石头砸自己脚了，你要收敛上生产\"。第 1 步：引用检查搬进正式代码 `src/hivemind/baseline.py`，加\"行名是报告的、数在同一行就存原文那一整行\"的修复（漏脚注记号、跳格）；对照 36 例全对，三个弄坏的版本各抓出 1 个错；重放全部存下的读法，改变的正好是那 6 个被拒的对数。第 2 步：第三版加修好的检查读 8 月留出财报 132 次（0.096 美元），两人分类 | 第 1 步：只改了那 6 条。第 2 步过：44 个数 0 个错（3 条\"剩余资本开支承诺 70 亿\"两人不一致，对着原文定为\"自己的量，别的期间\"）；v10 3/3、v12 2/3 | 读法定为第三版加修好的检查，不再改；第 3 步写正式代码 |\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n**The one next task: Alex's answer on the hybrid's release line (D681–D688, 2026-11-20).** Alex opened the hybrid's build and\ntest, and asked that problems not be found only at the end (his words are in the D681 record). Plan: [PLAN.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md). Design:\n[DESIGN-J2.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md).\n- **Where old loses on the 32 matters:**\n  - it never opens 17;\n  - it opened M08 and M14 in 3/3 draws, but the judge reasoned wrongly: amounts that overlap were added, and a figure of another scope\n    was taken as the answer.\n- **Census:** 24 answers rejected by both readers ([CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/census/CENSUS.md)).\n- **Found at $0:** the judge writes the rung first and its reference and derivation last (`schema_for` appends the stance fields to\n  the end of `properties`).\n- **Arms:**\n  - J2a, the schema order only;\n  - J2b, J2a plus an overlap and scope check.\n- **The probe and its rule** are written before any J2 send. Its regression guard is the frozen judgement gold: the stored v7 requests\n  give 15/17, 15/17 and 16/17, and are rebuilt byte for byte.\n- **Status (D685):**\n  - **The judge line is paused within D198.** Four angles have failed:\n    - J2a and J2b fail the locked blind reading;\n    - removing the previous conclusion misses its screen by one, and the frozen gold reads 44.3 against 45.0;\n    - H1, the heading only, gives 0 net repairs against 2 in council J's blind diagnostic.\n  - The carried derivation holds the rejected rungs. Every remaining lever changes D198.\n  - **No fresh test exists on this corpus.** The judge's errors sit in about ten numeric bets the design has read; 27 fresh bets gave\n    1 target against 8 needed.\n- **Opening census (D686):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md). Of the 16 matters old never opens:\n  - 6 are merged into a held question, because the scoring list is finer than D197 and D248;\n  - 5 fall outside the library's NVIDIA-only subject;\n  - 5, plus M05, are never proposed, though D248 allows them; a fix needs a new extraction version (D274).\n- **D382 answered (D687; his words are in the record):** in the hybrid, a company's own material figure keeps its own question, as\n  old's opening does.\n- **Attainable check (D688, council M):** [OPENING-CENSUS.md](research/2026-11-20-hybrid/OPENING-CENSUS.md), last two sections.\n  - The census found no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone.\n  - The concrete misses within Alex's rules are M20 (a $125B unsigned obligation, D388) and M05. M09, M30 and M25 are coin flips.\n  - Noise costs about 1.4.\n  - What binds: the list counts finer than D248/D388 on 9 matters, the NVIDIA-only subject on 5, and D198 on 2.\n  - No opening test is sent.\n- **Waiting on Alex (D688):**\n  - The recommendation: keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. The judge and reading fixes stay quality\n    work.\n  - Questions on other research-list companies' key figures are offered only for their own value.\n  - Spend so far: phase 1 $2.4 of $3; `phase1b` $0.36 of $2.\n5:record cold and do not assume earlier conclusions are right, including Claude's.\n26:  - The judge is judging-v7 (D354). Alex opened a new judge version, J2, in D681.\n27:  - D198 (what the judge reads: the evidence in view, and a previous conclusion that \"carries\" the rest) is Alex's decision.\n34:  - D682 opened the `phase1b` ledger \"inside D439's $40\".\n35:  - Ledgers: `poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/ledger/phase1.json` ($2.64 of $3) and `phase1b.json` ($0.36 of $2).\n52:- The judge's prompt and the code that builds its request: search `src/hivemind/` for \"Previous conclusion\" and `build_prompt`.\n55:1. **The judge.** Four angles failed (J2a, J2b, removing the previous conclusion, H1 the heading only). Is the remaining evidence a\n57:   - What is established: 0 of 13 move with the previous conclusion even on full evidence; 8 of 13 move without it, with 0 of 8\n65:2. **Untested within D198:** moving the previous conclusion earlier in the request (named by reflection K). Is it a sourced lever, or\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
