{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"The stored test shows that repeating the old reasoning can keep a bad forecast in place. Removing it helped some answers and hurt the China-share answer, so I’m checking whether there’s a way to test a safer change without reusing the same examples."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt; rg -n '\"'^## D(370|374|388|389|359)'\"\\\\b|\"'^## .*defect'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '488,552p'; find poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window -type f | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/prompts/judging-v7.txt; rg -n '\"'^## D(370|374|388|389|359)'\"\\\\b|\"'^## .*defect'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '488,552p'; find poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window -type f | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging a thesis's current rung. Use only the supplied evidence, dependency conclusions and themes in force. The rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Rejudge from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently), the current conclusions of dependencies and the themes in force. Pieces in force that no recent judgement relied on are not shown; the previous conclusion carries them. Do not add to or subtract from the previous score. The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison.\n     4\t- Judge against a reference: what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on the ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted by default; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. State the implied figure or date, check it against the dependencies' conclusions shown (a part cannot exceed its whole, and a figure that spans several periods or products gives this question only its share), compare it with the rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input to be discounted for time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say), not an answer; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- “Themes in force” lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on this thesis and report it in theme_pushes with the direction it pushes this thesis (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked “updated since this thesis was last judged” may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- A dependency marked “not yet created” supplies no input. A dependency marked “historical only” is closed without a successor; its closing conclusion is background only.\n     9\t- Your conclusion must be consistent with the conclusions of the theses it depends on and the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open; a component cannot exceed its whole.\n    10\t- Return the rung's one-based position; reference (what the market expects and which rung that is); implied_outcome (the figure or date the evidence implies and how you derived it, in one or two sentences); reasons (the gap between the two and why it does or does not cross a rung boundary); citations to supplied evidence and dependency IDs; each evidence item's push (toward_first, toward_last or none); theme_pushes; changed; and why_changed. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n    11\t- changed is true for a different rung or a change to the key facts or figures supporting the same rung, including a changed implied outcome. Repetition or another source for the same statement does not alone change the conclusion. The first judgement always has changed true.\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:140:## Open defects\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3711:## D355 · 2026-11-04 · The filing topic closes without a change: filing is about 85% right; the remaining misses are recorded as known defects\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3798:## D359 · 2026-11-04 · The code builds only the frozen prompts (extraction v74i, judging-v7); old worktrees removed; the preflight reads the one-decider requests\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3998:## D370 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Remove the separate earnings-report import\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4027:## D374 · 2026-11-05 · Remove the misleading sampling setting\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4172:## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4185:## D389 · 2026-11-09 · An unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question at about 5% of the company's annual profit\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4831:## D434 · 2026-11-13 · After c14's failed stage 1: finish diagnosing Step 1's other defects, then change them together\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7216:## D566 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the D520 line closed with its record for Alex; a production closing defect fixed; the new system's daily loop to close due questions as production does (council consensus, rounds 17 to 24)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7357:## D574 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: a freshly opened page shows the served library's latest completed day; the first day of a live store is an open defect; next, the live-service design (council consensus, rounds 45 to 50)\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8231:## D615 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 154): the period split is developed at $0 as a lead on D397's open defect; no gate movement claimed, no probe authorized\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9158:## D656 · 2026-11-17 · The paired test of v5.5 (D655): FAIL by the prewritten rule; D654's class recovered on the exposed targets; v5.5 kept as an unaccepted candidate; next, a $0 census of the listing defect\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9273:## D661 · 2026-11-17 · Open defect: the Codex-family blind readers ran with Codex memories on, which carry project context\n   488\t\n   489\t**Earlier next task, closed by D676 and D677 (D665–D675): read the release comparison's six draws when they finish, with the council-reviewed tools**\n   490\t(`docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v12.md` §1.4–§1.6; `DESIGN-1.6.md` v7; D675).\n   491\t\n   492\t- **Done:**\n   493\t  - stage 0 and slice 2;\n   494\t  - the full run, six draws, launched together at 22:36 on 2026-11-17 under `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/`;\n   495\t  - every reading instrument built and passed by the council before any output was read: reading tools in round 5, the §1.6 tools in\n   496\t    round 10; the scorer hardened through Codex rounds 11–21 (D675); 101 stage0 tests, 75 mutants on the reading tools.\n   497\t- **Result, 2026-11-19 (diagnostic, 5 draws; Alex stopped new-1).** The new system loses on the release comparison.\n   498\t  - Of 32 key matters, the new system serves 2–3 and the old one 10 (a = 0, b = 7–8). The controls pass.\n   499\t  - Even a perfect new-1 could not reverse it.\n   500\t  - The new libraries miss the core revenue, margin and capex matters.\n   501\t  - Details: `docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-LOG.md`, `poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/reading-diagnostic/`.\n   502\t  - **Diagnosed (D676, council):** D382's figure exclusion plus the Step 1→ladder bundled-question loss (D432). Even repaired, the new system ties at best. The old system stays; no further comparison run.\n   503\t  - **The goal loop is closed (D677, council).** The old system stays and no paid work continues. It reopens only if Alex reverses D505\n   504\t    or funds a full run, with a written path to passing first.\n   505\t  - **The one-outcome probe failed its line 1** (`docs/research/2026-11-19-one-outcome-probe/RESULT.md`): it fixes the period bundles\n   506\t    but not the deal bundles.\n   507\t  - **What a pass would take** ($0 arithmetic on the frozen list; pass = a − b ≥ 5 and a ≥ 2b):\n   508\t    - **Under D382:** the old system keeps 4 figure matters the new one can never take, so b ≥ 4. The new system would need at least 9\n   509\t      matters only it serves, out of the 14 its rules allow that the old system misses: 6 shared quantities, 5 obligations and 3\n   510\t      policy steps. Today it serves 0–1 of them.\n   511\t    - **With D382 reversed:** at least 5 of 17, the 14 plus 3 figures the old system misses, provided it also matches the old system on\n   512\t      the rest.\n   513\t    - **Either way:** passing needs much broader opening, not a wording fix.\n   514\t- **(Superseded) When all six draws end, in this order:**\n   515\t  1. `eligibility.py`: six complete draws, launched within 1 h, sends within 72 h.\n   516\t  2. `mapping.py export`, then `read`, `third`, `result`.\n   517\t  3. `mark_cards.py deck`, then `mark`, `debate 1`, `debate 2`, `readings`.\n   518\t  4. `score_comparison.py <run root> <mapping out> <marks folder>`: rebuilds every derived file from the primary data (refuses any that\n   519\t     differs, the readings record included) and gives the verdict and the printed-beside quantities on the rebuilt snapshot.\n   520\t  5. `d400_code_check.py` and `step2_lines.py`: the hard checks and the release status.\n   521\t  6. `d400_reader_lines.py` and `d431_reading.py`: printed beside.\n   522\t  7. A council loop on the result, and a row in `TRIES.md`.\n   523\t- **If a draw stops:** no release verdict; a diagnostic export (plan §1.4 item 10).\n   524\t- **If the verdict is not a practical lead:** the council-loop skill on the traces, and the next try from another angle (D674).\n   525\t- **Monitored** in `RUN-LOG.md`. Out-of-scope findings go to `FINDINGS.md`.\n   526\t- **Held** (D662): answer-choice changes, model trials, and live-store, planner and integration work. D658 waits (D664).\n   527\t- **Open:** D661 (past Codex readers ran with memories on); D656's listing omission; the 589 uncommitted paths (his call).\n   528\t\n   529\t**After D638:** the stop hook rejected the hold, so the council opened D612's fourth condition with a new candidate, astra with arm A2\n   530\t(D436's second-side sentences; D639).\n   531\t- **Two readings,** both VOID by their planted listing controls (D640, D641).\n   532\t- **Descriptive only:**\n   533\t  - A2 wrote H20 2 of 2 where the frozen arm declined 2 of 2, unflagged by both product reviewers;\n   534\t  - memory is disputed;\n   535\t  - agreed hard-line failures frozen 2 against A2 0;\n   536\t  - the listing harm is unmeasured.\n   537\t- **Its status:** astra with A2 stays provisional and unadopted, and the route stops.\n   538\t\n   539\t**The state, measured today** (`reflection-6/`, D623 to D637):\n   540\t- **The readers are valid** (D625).\n   541\t- **Higher effort and a required field are closed** (D626), and so is a paired gate-3 comparison (D628).\n   542\t- **Sol** fails 9 of 78 sends on the 26 topics outside the 44. **Astra**, on the unchanged request, fails 4 of 78, all main-part\n   543\t  declines (D633, D634).\n   544\t- **The main-part choice is unsourced** (D631). Two rule candidates closed (D631, D635). Six cases are on Alex's page.\n   545\t- **A source-backed review of astra's 51 written questions** finds 11 material defects that gate 1 does not count (D636).\n   546\t- **A one-clause correction** (`due-day/candidate-system-v2.txt`, the binding-obligation day narrowed to amounts per D210 and D403)\n   547\t  fixes the signed-deal completion date in its probe, 4 of 4 against 0 of 4, with no control moved.\n   548\t  - Its verdict is inconclusive on one unrelated listing split (D637).\n   549\t  - It is kept beside the frozen request, unadopted.\n   550\t- **Two leads closed at $0:** the MIIT listing (request-independent) and the purchase-commitment ranges (the recorded fixed-range\n   551\t  limitation).\n   552\t- **A third lead closed (D638):** Rubin's widened window follows the topic's own period field, which contradicts its description. It\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window/old-2/replay/days.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window/old-2/replay/results.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window/old-2/replay/checks.json\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window/old-2/replay/archive.sqlite\npoc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/window/old-2/replay/views.sqlite\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'old-[123].*(views|ledger)|def .*older|store_path|db_path' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/{judge_probe,fresh_test,window_replay,opening_census}.py; rg -n 'C100|Q7|Q16|Q37' poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/fullscore.json; rg -n '\"'^(#|'\"\\\\*\\\\*|##)' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-*-codex.md | head -75\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'old-[123].*(views|ledger)|def .*older|store_path|db_path' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/{judge_probe,fresh_test,window_replay,opening_census}.py; rg -n 'C100|Q7|Q16|Q37' poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/fullscore.json; rg -n '\"'^(#|'\"\\\\*\\\\*|##)' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-*-codex.md | head -75\"","aggregated_output":"rg: docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/window_replay.py: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:78:    _, archive = jp.store_paths(draw)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:92:        views, _ = jp.store_paths(draw)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:148:        views, archive = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:167:    views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:196:def write_deck(folder, key_path, cards, confirmations, seed):\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:307:            views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:386:                if answer['rung'] not in builder.bc.conditions(case['view_id'], builder.bc.ro(jp.store_paths(case['draw'])[0])):\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py:426:            views, _ = jp.store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/opening_census.py:25:    views, _ = jp.store_paths(draw)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:73:def store_paths(draw):\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:121:    views, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:379:    views, _ = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:384:def expected_files(folder, names, repeats=3):\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:545:        views, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:745:        views, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:775:        _, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:779:        views, _ = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:930:        views, _ = store_paths(case['draw'])\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:973:            views, _ = store_paths(case['draw'])\n11:  \"T-old-1-Q7\",\n12:  \"T-old-2-Q16\",\n13:  \"T-old-3-Q37\",\n14:  \"T-old-3-Q7\"\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-c-codex.md:1:**Hold J2. The refusal check misclassified four of 117 stored v7 re-sends.** It reads the archived final judgement as the previous one. All three Q31 re-sends stayed at the range shown in their request, but the harness flagged them as moves. That inflates v7’s refusal count and makes rule (d) easier for J2 to pass. Validate against the state immediately before each request. [judge_probe.py:329](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:329) · [judging.py:226](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:226)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-m-codex.md:1:**Skip a release comparison. Diagnose the opening misses that the existing rules already cover.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-a-codex.md:1:**Hold J2 before sending.** Putting the reasoning first is worth testing. J2b could make the judge ignore valid estimates, and the probe could miss that regression.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-b-codex.md:1:**Hold the J2 sends.** The deck builder still samples eight unchanged-range answers per arm. That can hide better or worse reasoning within the same range. Require all 432 repeats to be accounted for, and count production refusals before scoring. [judge_probe.py:330](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:330)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-l-codex.md:1:**Fix the census before treating its ceiling as a product limit.** Some missing questions fit Alex’s existing rules.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-h-codex.md:1:**Both J2 failures stand. One reader call could change the separating test by a point, and the frozen gold regression stands independently.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-m2-codex.md:1:**Keep old in production and pause the hybrid release line.** No opening send currently earns its cost. I agree with that exit, with two corrections to the census.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-m2-codex.md:8:**Recommend option 2 to Alex.** Five speculative gains with zero losses can pass mathematically. The two concrete opportunities cannot carry that result. Drop the M20 account probe for release purposes. Widen company coverage only if Alex wants those forecasts for their own value. D543 supports closing the release investigation when another test would leave the decision unchanged. [D543](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6604)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-d-codex.md:1:**Two gaps remain.** I reproduced 0/144 v7 probe refusals, 3/153 gold refusals, and strict gold agreement of 45, 46 and 42 out of 51. The coverage check rejects missing files. [judge_probe.py:336](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py:336)\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-j-codex.md:1:**Send a five-case H1 diagnostic. The fresh test correctly stopped at one target.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-m3-codex.md:1:**Keep poc-v118 in production and pause the hybrid release line.** D688 needs one wording change. Say “the census found no credible path to a D665 lead through opening changes alone.” Five gains with zero losses would pass on paper, but only M20 and M05 are concrete opportunities, and the roughly 1.4 losses are an estimate.\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-i-codex.md:1:**Hold the send. The pool contains questions the design already saw, and the scorer can credit an answer production would refuse.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-g-codex.md:1:**Stop J2a and J2b as candidates. Result 3 shows that removing the previous answer changes forecasts. It leaves open whether those changes improve them.**\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-f-codex.md:1:**The carried answer is a plausible influence. The fork cannot isolate it.**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
