{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/CURRENT_STATE.md | sed -n '138,171p'; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '3998,4012p;4172,4200p'; sed -n '67,93p' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py; ls poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/goldprobe\"","aggregated_output":"   138\t- **Repository:** `main` holds the product, the frozen ruler and the research records; run databases, logs and model archives stay on disk (D353), located by the [data manifest](research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md). Worktrees: `/Users/lchingen/hivemind` is the main checkout, where slice branches are cut from `main`; `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28` (the extraction branch, merged on 2026-11-03) keeps in its ignored folders the stored end-to-end runs of `poc-v91` to `poc-v95` that later comparisons read (D359); `/Users/lchingen/hivemind-run-v109-2026-11-04` is the finished judging-v8 run's worktree. Older branches stay in Git without worktrees (D359); none is merged work in progress. The clean source-text comparison and its condition-hidden review are complete; council discussion of next steps is ongoing.\n   139\t\n   140\t## Open defects\n   141\t\n   142\t1. **Competitor and customer news is filed under the company's revenue questions** instead of the share, capital-spending or custom-chip question it informs (D355; filing is otherwise about 85% right). Share facts are often not written at all, an extraction recall miss. The total-revenue question holds about a quarter of all links (D354).\n   143\t2. **One bet opened twice** about one encounter in five: the collision judge splits a seed question from an identical candidate on a fine detail (D354).\n   144\t3. **A question the standard rules out** (the lidar legislation) was proposed by the extraction and opened in one draw of three (D354).\n   145\t4. **A thesis opened from an article gets no dependency of its own**: the default Jev matching asks for none (`views/jev_matching.py`), although D51 has the matching call choose them; themes still reach every company thesis through the theme block (D191, D195). Found in the 2026-11-05 consolidation; building it is decided (D368).\n   146\t5. **Historical coverage-start reading, retired by D370** (D364–D366): the capital-spending line is missed in about one read in six (the question is then left as it was); a labelled guidance figure is written with the fact tier; later reports reach the questions only through the daily stream; `scripts/preflight.py` does not replay the reading's check.\n   147\t6. **Measured on one company and one 14-day window**, the judgement scored at the window end only; no version of the current pipeline has completed a longer window (a 60-day run of `poc-v108` was stopped at Alex's word after 2026-07-15, [log row 8](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)). The China-share question (v17) swings between draws (0 of 3 in the acceptance, 2 of 3 in its control, 1 of 3 in the frozen draws): two readers found the starting figures did not cause the acceptance's drop, and the byte-identical extraction request kept a \"share fell to zero\" sentence in two candidate draws and dropped it in two control draws. One acceptance draw judged nothing on v16; its cause is not established.\n   148\t7. **What a judgement reads grows with the window** (D358). Argument records (D201) were measured as the remedy on 2026-11-04 and not built: judging-v8 agreed 12 of 17 against 15 of 17, judging-v9's card added little at about half again the judging cost; their code was removed at Alex's request ([log rows 4–11](research/2026-11-04-argument-record/log.md)).\n   149\t8. **Seen once, not traced.** A judgement named a shown theme as a dependency and the check refused it twice, stopping a draw for a day (2026-11-02, D266). The sealed run's review recorded that a succession's opening evidence is not linked to the new question (D358), not yet checked against today's code.\n   150\t9. **Earlier defects, unchanged.** Matching (build log row 49): another document's copy of a figure can be treated as new evidence; one matter can occupy several groups; same-answer candidate references caused seven chain or duplication decisions of the generative matcher; empty `original_who` values can count as the same party; different names for one population cause two of nine Jev merge misses. Nine 2026 aggregate-spending theses under `ai-capex` each have a different population; whether to combine them is a product choice. Extraction's instructions remain narrower than the PRD's important-question rule and omit the personal-memo exception, and extraction can change a quantity's meaning before matching (a guarantee amount against financing provided). Classification keeps its [recorded simulation defects](research/2026-10-25-english/classification-existing-defects.txt). The corpus audit recorded 97 official notices with 56 body and file-name collisions, to re-fetch before relying on a rebuilt corpus. An older intermittent search-test failure is untraced. Fresh Idea allocations vary while saved weights do not; the confidence chart applies the current plan to past states and is not a calibrated probability; broad analyst-prose quality and fresh Idea stability remain unaccepted (the [Idea contract](poc/idea-card.md) lists its limits); generative matching dependencies await `matching-v4`. The readers' doubts about the frozen standard, listed in the [extraction branch's state page](research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/current-state-extraction-branch-2026-11-03.md), remain for Alex.\n   151\t\n   152\tUpstream supply and the human review pool's output remain deferred.\n   153\t\n   154\t10. **A new-system store being written serves its first day in progress** (D573, D574; `docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/page-contract/LIVE-READ-DESIGN.md`, B):\n   155\t   before any day completes, the service's default date falls back to the latest judgement's day. Not built: a correct guard needs one\n   156\t   snapshot for the check and the read, MCP's start and the streamed Idea response handled; 0 of 143 stores are in that state and no\n   157\t   new-system store is served live today.\n   158\t\n   159\t## One next task\n   160\t\n   161\t**Where the lean path stands (2026-11-15; D489 to D542).** Alex is not active (D509); D439 is in force: choices go to the\n   162\tcouncil (an independent Codex review and Claude) until consensus, recorded citing D439; nothing is pushed, deployed, published or\n   163\tcommitted; paid calls stay within D439's $40 ceiling (about $18.42 recorded; $0.0134 sent in this period, the ten judge calls of\n   164\tD511 and D519; the lean path $8.34 in all). Every stretch below is closed; its full record is in the decision log and in\n   165\t`research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/LEAN-LOG.md` (sections 1 to 43).\n   166\t\n   167\t- **The choice between the systems is not made.** The fresh week did not separate them (D489, \"not clear\"; nothing since ranks\n   168\t  them). The comparison that could choose by measurement was sized and not sent: at the proposed size it may miss differences\n   169\t  that matter ([sizing](research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison/COMPARISON-SIZING.md), D517). **Production stays the default\n   170\t  and both systems stay (D518).** Alex's product choice on the company's financial figures stands (D505: evidence for related\n   171\t  questions, no table and no questions of their own; D382 and D384 stand).\n  3998\t## D370 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Remove the separate earnings-report import\n  3999\t\n  4000\t- Alex: “我觉得财报这个基本是没有的，我觉得可以记录下，删除这个财报倒入的环节。重新整理现在的系统设计”. He also previously directed removal of the 22 artificial preset questions and confirmed that extraction should read the existing research library.\n  4001\t- Remove the separate coverage-start report reading tied to seeded questions and do not add an earnings report as background to each news extraction request. This supersedes D363–D366 to the extent they require that separate report import and seeded default. An earnings release or filing arriving as an actual input remains a normal item under D28; existing research questions remain extraction context. Historical seeds, gold, results and records remain historical, not a new active starting library.\n  4002\t- Evidence is bounded: a diagnostic with three archived NVDA articles, the same 68-question 2026-08-28 library, two arms and three draws gave 14/27 complete matters without the appended report versus 13/27 with it; one report-arm answer supplied an unestablished CFO statement date. This tested adding a report to extraction, not the distinct D363–D366 coverage-start mechanism; the removal of both is Alex's decision, not a claim that the experiment directly tested both. The library is historical and not the complete article-day state. See `../hivemind-no-preseed-evidence-review/docs/research/2026-11-05-real-input-evidence/existing-library-results-2026-11-05.md` in the local worktree.\n  4003\t- Implementation and rollout status must be stated separately from this decision. The frozen earlier rulers and scores stay unchanged; no conclusion about other companies or report-as-source inputs is implied.\n  4004\t\n  4005\t\n  4006\t## D371 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Track present and forward-looking financial information\n  4007\t\n  4008\t- Alex: “收入和财务这边对于当下，未来应该都是需要track 的，你应该要修改”. This is the product decision for the financial extraction and filing issue discussed immediately before it.\n  4009\t- Present and forward-looking financial performance, estimates and guidance need to be tracked as evidence relevant to investment questions; a quarterly period is not itself a reason to withhold information from a related annual question. Do not confuse retaining and connecting evidence with automatically opening a separate question for every line. The research model continues to judge relevance and the strength of the connection; do not hard-code company, item or metric-specific importance. Existing research questions remain context; the separate report import and 22 preset questions remain retired under D370.\n  4010\t- The frozen earlier standard, gold and scores remain unchanged. Where the new decision changes how present financial context is treated, use a dated decision/correction and a separately versioned evaluation; never silently relabel old gold or compare scores across rulers. Implementation and diagnostic evidence must be recorded separately.\n  4011\t\n  4012\t## D372 · 2026-11-05 UTC · Score future evidence by usefulness, not core versus supporting\n  4172\t## D388 · 2026-11-09 · A material unsigned obligation gets its own signing question beside an open total of its kind\n  4173\t\n  4174\t- Asked: \"一笔重大的、还没签的承诺（比如为 OpenAI 俄亥俄数据中心租约做担保），要不要在已有的'担保总额'问题之外，单独开一个'会不会签'的问题？\"\n  4175\t  Alex chose \"单独开 (Recommended)\".\n  4176\t- **Decided.** A material unsigned obligation that merits a separate investment judgment keeps its own yes/no question on whether\n  4177\t  it is signed by the check date, beside an open question on the total of the same kind. This confirms D248 boundary 1's exception,\n  4178\t  which had not been put to him. A small unsigned obligation, or a deal already signed under a plan tracked by amount, stays evidence\n  4179\t  for the total.\n  4180\t- **Why it matters now.** The c8 dev draws fold the Ohio guarantee into the aggregate in 3 of 3, and q23 of the frozen judgement gold\n  4181\t  asks it. Arm c9 showed that a sentence-level rule flips by send (round log §§48–50).\n  4182\t- **Next.** A structural lever, designed and reviewed by the council before any send. c8 stays in force until a version is shown to\n  4183\t  be better on new, unused articles.\n  4184\t\n  4185\t## D389 · 2026-11-09 · An unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question at about 5% of the company's annual profit\n  4186\t\n  4187\t- Asked: \"“多大算大”用什么尺寸？\" The options were 5% of a year's profit (recommended), 1% of annual revenue, or no threshold and stop.\n  4188\t  Alex chose \"一年利润的 5% (Recommended)\", whose stated terms were:\n  4189\t  - \"单笔未签承诺约达到公司一年利润的 5% 才单独开'会不会签'（亏损公司另议）\";\n  4190\t  - \"金额不知道的，比如俄亥俄，仍按文章描述定性判断\";\n  4191\t  - \"公司最近一年利润作为固定资料交给小步骤\".\n  4192\t- **Decided.** Under D388, a single unsigned obligation is large enough for its own signing question when its stated amount is about 5%\n  4193\t  or more of the company's most recent annual profit. An obligation whose amount is not stated is judged qualitatively from what the\n  4194\t  item states. The company's most recent annual profit is supplied to the step as fixed input, with its source. A loss-making company\n  4195\t  is not covered and is decided when one arises.\n  4196\t- **Why.** In the focused D388 call, the same $2bn stake opened in 0 of 3 draws under one wording and 3 of 3 under another, and a\n  4197\t  $2.5–3bn stake opened in 6 of 6, even when compared with stated revenue (round log §§54–55). The standard's \"large enough to change\"\n  4198\t  (D248 boundary 6) had no anchor the model applied consistently. The 5% line agrees with every known verdict:\n  4199\t  - small: about $2bn, $2.5–3bn, Intel's $5bn;\n  4200\t  - open: Hugging Face at $12.9bn.\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    return module\n\n\ndef store_paths(draw):\n    \"\"\"(views, archive) of a finished comparison draw, as the comparison's mapping read them.\"\"\"\n    root = RUN / draw\n    record = json.loads((root / 'run.json').read_text())\n    if draw.startswith('new'):\n        judge = record['components']['judge']\n        inner = json.loads((root / judge['folder'] / 'run.json').read_text())[draw]\n        folder = root / judge['folder'] / inner['attempts'][-1]['folder']\n    else:\n        folder = root / record['components']['prod']['folder']\n    return folder / 'views.sqlite', folder / 'archive.sqlite'\n\n\ndef readonly(path):\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{path}?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n    return conn\n\n\ndef cases():\n    \"\"\"Targets, and per target one control from the same draw and of the same type that both readers marked worth tracking and\nJ2a\nJ2b\nv7\nv7-noprev\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '188,208p' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md; sed -n '1,33p' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/reflection-k-claude.md; sed -n '1,28p' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/fresh_test.py; rg -n 'J2a|same-day|Cost' docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py | head -25; ls -1 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"  - The cost is about $2 per draw and arm, from archived tokens.\n  - It replaces the slice from the 09-06 copy, which carried every earlier wrong rung.\n\n## Result 2: the frozen judgement gold, rule (c) (51 requests × 3, scored by the frozen scorer's rule)\n| Arm | Agreement per repeat (of 51) | Mean | Strict (refused counted as not agreeing) | Refused (of 153) | Rule (c): mean no lower than v7's |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| v7 re-send | 45, 46, 44 | 45.0 | 45, 46, 42 (44.3) | 3 | — |\n| J2a | 44, 44, 45 | 44.3 | 43, 44, 45 (44.0) | 1 | **missed** |\n| J2b | 44, 45, 45 | 44.7 | 44, 44, 44 (44.0) | 2 | **missed** |\n\n- **The questions that differ, read with their reasons.**\n  - Five are single-repeat flips on boundary questions: d1-q17 and d3-q17 (China share), d2-q08 (H200 authorization), d2-q22 and\n    d3-q22 (FY2028 revenue).\n  - **One is a consistent J2b regression: d3-q18**, Kyber NVL144 shipping by the end of 2027. The gold says No (the reported slip to\n    2028). v7 says No in 2 of 3 repeats; J2b says Yes in 3 of 3. J2b's reasons treat the slip report as \"one underlying source\", weigh\n    NVIDIA's denial, and name the NVL576 statement \"a proxy\". The scope row was read as a reason to discount specific third-party\n    evidence. That is the direction council A warned of.\n- **Both arms miss (c) as written.** The gaps are within one question of 51, inside v7's own repeat range of 44–46. The miss stands as\n  scored.\n\n## The whole-window production path (validated at $0)\n# Reflection K: Claude's own, written before the cold reader's (2026-11-20)\n\n**Facts.**\n- **H1 (heading only)** fails council J's diagnostic: 0 net repairs against 2 required. v7 left 3 targets to repair, so the result is\n  conclusive. No control was lost, no refusals, and both plants were caught. By code, H1 kept the rejected rung in 8 of 9 target\n  answers; same-day v7 kept it in 7 of 9. The label does not matter. The content of the carried conclusion does: with it, 0 of 13\n  targets moved even on complete evidence; without it, 8 of 13 moved.\n- **Four angles on the judge have failed:** J2a (schema order), J2b (a check), the removal of the previous conclusion (screen missed by\n  one, gold 44.3 against 45.0), and H1.\n\n**Lessons, at the level of mechanism.**\n1. The anchor is the carried derivation itself. A label or an instruction around it does not loosen it.\n2. **Every remaining lever changes D198, which is Alex's decision.** The levers are:\n   - show the rung without the derivation;\n   - replace the derivation with a summary of the omitted evidence;\n   - show all evidence.\n\n   \"All evidence\" cannot scale: one question carries 2,264 pieces in force. That is why D198 clips.\n3. **The fresh census shows where the judge's errors sit.** They are in about ten big numeric bets, and the design has read all of\n   them. Yes/no completion questions are mostly right. Any judge change can be tested freshly only on a new window.\n\n**Weaker than they look.**\n- The 4 net repairs without the previous conclusion are dev.\n- Gold 44.3 against 45.0 sits inside v7's own range of 44–46.\n- C100 is not yet rechecked.\n- The judge's attainable gain on the 32 matters is M08 and M14 at most, so +2 matters.\n\n**Remaining problems, by product impact (PLAN, \"Attainable\").**\n1. **Opening:** 17 of 32 matters are never opened, and 3 more are opened in only 1 of 3 draws. This is the release's gap.\n2. **D382** (company-figure questions): 5 to 6 matters, open with Alex.\n3. **The judge:** at most 2 matters, and only through a change to D198.\n\n**The next angle.**\n\"\"\"The fresh test of a presentation-only change to the previous conclusion (council H, D684), on answers the design never read.\n\n  python3 fresh_test.py pool                       # $0: freshpool.json; every pooled request rebuilt byte for byte under the frozen judge\n  python3 fresh_test.py censusdeck                 # $0 + plant confirmations: blind cards of every pooled answer as stored\n  python3 fresh_test.py censusread                 # both reader families mark the census deck, rounds 0-2 (no API spend)\n  python3 fresh_test.py select                     # $0: freshcases.json by the rule written in DESIGN-J2.md before any reading\n  python3 fresh_test.py check [pool]               # $0: each arm's request built, the heading replaced exactly once, a synthetic answer checked\n  python3 fresh_test.py probe <ledger> <arm> <k>   # cents: each fresh case's request under the arm, sent k times\n  python3 fresh_test.py gold <ledger> <arm> <k>    # cents: the frozen judgement gold's requests under the arm\n  python3 fresh_test.py testdeck <arm> [<arm> ...] # $0 + plant confirmations: blind cards of every answer of every arm and repeat\n  python3 fresh_test.py testread                   # both reader families mark the test deck\n  python3 fresh_test.py score <arm>                # $0: the screen, the arm against the same-day v7 re-send\n\nThe pool: per draw of the release comparison and per question of its library, the latest judgement on or before CUT (the day before the\ndev window), unless the design read an answer of that question in that draw (the 24 targets, their 24 controls, the 49 census answers),\nthe question's last judgement is that same one (its answer was read at 09-20), it is a first judgement (no previous conclusion), or it is\na retry. Stores are read through read-only connections; keys stay outside the repository.\"\"\"\nimport concurrent.futures\nimport json\nimport math\nimport random\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\n627:    one; any other arm sends, with an empty archive of its own (council B: J2a and v7 share an archive key).\"\"\"\n693:def probescore(arms=('v7', 'J2a', 'J2b')):\n791:def forkscore(arms=('v7', 'J2a', 'J2b')):\ncouncil-j-codex.md\ncouncil-j-codex.stream\ncouncil-l-brief.md\ncouncil-l-codex.md\ncouncil-l-codex.stream\ncouncil-m-brief.md\ncouncil-m-codex.md\ncouncil-m-codex.stream\ncouncil-m-round2-brief.md\ncouncil-m-round3-brief.md\ncouncil-m2-codex.md\ncouncil-m2-codex.stream\ncouncil-m3-codex.md\ncouncil-m3-codex.stream\ncouncil-n-brief.md\ncouncil-n-codex.md\ncouncil-n-codex.stream\nfresh-bets.json\nfresh_test.py\njudge_probe.py\nopening_census.py\nreflection-k-brief.md\nreflection-k-claude.md\nreflection-k-codex.md\nreflection-k-codex.stream\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import pathlib,json,collections as c; p=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20\\\"); cs=json.loads((p/\\\"fullcases.json\\\").read_text()); print(\\\"coverage\\\",len(cs),c.Counter(x[\\\"role\\\"] for x in cs)); print(\\\"fresh\\\",len(json.loads((p/\\\"freshpool.json\\\").read_text()))); print(\\\"window\\\",[(f,len(a:=json.loads((p/f).read_text())),sum(x[\\\"same text\\\"] for x in a),sum(x[\\\"same evidence shown\\\"] for x in a)) for f in [\\\"window/old-2/replay/checks.json\\\",\\\"prodpath/replay/checks.json\\\"]]); print(\\\"move\\\",[(a,c.Counter(x[\\\"role\\\"] for x in cs if sum(json.loads((p/\\\"probe\\\"/a/(x[\\\"case\\\"]+f\\\"-{i}.json\\\")).read_text())[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"rung\\\"]\"'!=x[\"rung\"] for i in [1,2,3])>=2)) for a in [\"v7-fullprev\",\"v7-fullnoprev\"]]);'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
