{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '6480,6588p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/judge_probe.py | sed -n '121,152p;917,952p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-brief.md | tail -29\"","aggregated_output":"  6480\t\n  6481\t- **The proof** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md`, `edge_proof.py`, $0): on scratch\n  6482\t  copies of the stored unseeded fresh week, the edge \"data-center revenue FY2027 depends on total revenue FY2027\" written by the\n  6483\t  writer's own steps. Judging, conditional on the rest of the week as stored: thirteen registered expectations hold (the reverse\n  6484\t  edge refused as a cycle; total revenue judged first; only the data-center request changes, by the dependency block holding\n  6485\t  total revenue's conclusion of the round cut at 600 characters and the closing sentence; the judge's check accepts the\n  6486\t  citation; every other judgement equal to the stored one); two mutants fail. Filing, every stored reading filed again by the\n  6487\t  production entry point (the control reproduces all 235 articles): through the narrowest rule in code (D265) the same edge\n  6488\t  removes the total-revenue link of seven statements: the company-wide outlook excluding China, which a total-revenue judgement\n  6489\t  cites and no other statement of it holds; three statements of the quarter's total and segment revenue in one sentence; three\n  6490\t  about the segment's competition (as the rule intends). An edge between an unrelated pair changes none.\n  6491\t- **The council's review:** the filing stop condition of D537 is met. A lost filing is not a demonstrated changed answer. The\n  6492\t  judging proof does not show a week with the edge present throughout. The selection slice (D368 item 2) cannot use the present\n  6493\t  edge behaviour unchanged; D368 already calls for separating the judging and filing uses for seed edges, and the proof extends\n  6494\t  the need to an article-created dependency. It decides no representation and does not authorize reversing D368's direction.\n  6495\t- **Decided, citing D439:** nothing is sent and no frozen piece changes. The dependency slice's design is opened at $0 for the\n  6496\t  council's review: the four tables of AGENTS §2, covering seed edges and matcher-chosen dependencies (a part reading its whole;\n  6497\t  a question reading a driver); the separate effects on filing, judging order, citations, propagation, cycles and later-added\n  6498\t  dependencies; the seven observed filing changes, a statement giving distinct figures for two questions, unrelated pairs and\n  6499\t  themes already covered by the theme block; D207, D259, D360 and D368's direction. Its first $0 proof must show the intended\n  6500\t  conclusion reaching the real judging path and the company-wide statement keeping its proper home, with unrelated filings\n  6501\t  unchanged and no cycle; if that cannot be shown under the existing decisions, stop and return the conflict, without fitting a\n  6502\t  special case. The six-call comparison stays deferred.\n  6503\t\n  6504\t## D539 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the separation of a dependency edge's two uses is kept as a candidate, not yet the builder's contract; its design continues at $0 (council consensus, reflection round 30)\n  6505\t\n  6506\t- **Reviewed** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md`, `separation_proof.py`): an edge\n  6507\t  carries a kind set by its writer (`supports`: a seed's driver and root, D208; `reads`: a dependency chosen for a question,\n  6508\t  D51 and PRD 06); judging reads one derived relation (a `reads` edge as written; a `supports` edge the other way round, D368\n  6509\t  item 4) and filing another (the driver of a `supports` edge is the narrower home; a `reads` edge states none). First proof,\n  6510\t  $0, 35 registered expectations: the unseeded fresh week's 235 filings unchanged with the `reads` edge and its last round\n  6511\t  showing the conclusion; a seeded draw's 243 filings unchanged and its last round ordered supporters first; circles refused.\n  6512\t- **The council's findings:** the proof passes its labelled examples and validates nothing more. Not applying D265's narrowest\n  6513\t  rule to a `reads` edge is a proposed interpretation with a trade-off, not a consequence D368 settles. The fresh-week result\n  6514\t  keeps double filing and does not show D207's one home satisfied. \"Kind is never inferred\" contradicted the table that read\n  6515\t  every old non-seed row as `reads`: the historical writers and ledgers must be inventoried and old rows given one explicit\n  6516\t  reading or refused, no ledger rewritten. The cycle rule had a counterexample: a `supports` edge and a `reads` edge in the\n  6517\t  same reading direction duplicate a reading and close no circle. The pages, the search records and the idea route expose the\n  6518\t  edge's meaning; the direction label is a blocker for a seeded build.\n  6519\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the separation stays a candidate. Continue its design at $0: the duplicate and old-row contracts,\n  6520\t  the D265 and D207 reading with its residual double filing stated, the reader and state tables completed, and a next proof\n  6521\t  that exercises both edge combinations and at least one real writer-and-reader path on a scratch store. Stop and return the\n  6522\t  conflict if the one-home requirement cannot be expressed without an unsupported new rule, or if the meaning of historical\n  6523\t  edges cannot be established. The selection call is not designed yet. No send; no frozen piece changed.\n  6524\t\n  6525\t## D540 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the separation stays a provisional research candidate; the filing and duplicate-label contracts are finished at $0 before any selection design or send (council consensus, reflection round 31)\n  6526\t\n  6527\t- **Reviewed:** the revised design and the second proof (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md`,\n  6528\t  `separation_proof_2.py`): the production seeding and writer steps, wrapped, store the kind of the edges they write; with the\n  6529\t  data-center revenue question's stored answers handed back, the whole unseeded fresh week keeps its stored filings and every\n  6530\t  other judgement while that question's seven requests gain total revenue's conclusion of the same round.\n  6531\t- **The council's findings:** not applying D265's narrowest rule to a chosen dependency is a reasonable provisional\n  6532\t  interpretation under D439, not a finished product rule and not an implementation of D207 and D360. A double link is not\n  6533\t  necessarily a reading error (D360 stores a two-figure sentence as one record linked to both questions); \"60 of 385\" sizes such\n  6534\t  records, not breaches. The second proof does not give the requests a live judge would produce: a real test runs each arm as a\n  6535\t  sequence from its own earlier answers. Two contracts still blocked calling the candidate sound: a proposed edge with the same\n  6536\t  reading pair and another direction label must not be discarded as a duplicate; and the inventory's claim must be bounded to\n  6537\t  the files and marks it read.\n  6538\t- **Decided, citing D439:** no judge call is sent. Finish at $0 the filing and duplicate-label contract: the seven observed\n  6539\t  statements, a single-figure driver-and-root case, a two-figure sentence and an unrelated pair, with the expected homes and the\n  6540\t  owner of each decision stated and no case-specific list in code; conflicting labels and unknown historical rows exercised.\n  6541\t  Stop and return to the council if the correct homes cannot be expressed under the existing decisions, or if resolving a label\n  6542\t  would require inventing its meaning.\n  6543\t\n  6544\t## D541 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the seed edge's label stops everything that touches a seed edge; the filing finding is bounded; the unseeded failure-and-reader contract is finished at $0 before the separation is called sound (council consensus, reflection round 32)\n  6545\t\n  6546\t- **Reviewed** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` sections 2.2, 2.3, 2.5;\n  6547\t  `filing_contract.py`; `separation_proof_2.py`, 20 registered expectations): ten filing cases run through the code's own rule\n  6548\t  (in every real case the reading step linked the statement to both questions; with no stated hierarchy five come out as the\n  6549\t  decisions call for, with one a different five); the outcomes for a second edge over an existing reading (the same label: not\n  6550\t  written; another label: a conflict, refused; over a seed edge: not comparable); the inventory bounded to 158 files and to\n  6551\t  marks.\n  6552\t- **The council's findings:** the seed-label stop has fired: `last_end`, written as a constant by the seeding module, is\n  6553\t  defined in no decision, page, seed file or prompt, and is given no meaning from its spelling; the stop covers the seeded\n  6554\t  reading and any comparison against a seed edge, not a separately bounded unseeded design. The filing stop has not fired: the\n  6555\t  expected homes are expressible under the existing decisions and not produced by an edge rule; the table is a hand reading of\n  6556\t  ten cases, and whether the company-wide outlook also bears on the segment stays open to review. Three gaps kept the unseeded\n  6557\t  contract from being called sound: a conflict seen only by the proof's helper, not by the production path, and a cycle\n  6558\t  described as a dropped note where PRD 06 says refuse and ask for a correction; old unseeded rows not shown through the\n  6559\t  service, search, bundle and idea readers; the everyday boundaries (a target closing or succeeded, an awaited target, a\n  6560\t  duplicate or conflict across articles, a theme already in the theme block).\n  6561\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the separation stays provisional. Finish the unseeded state-by-event and reader contracts at $0 and\n  6562\t  exercise the actual writer and readers on scratch stores, failure and resume included, a conflict observable; stop and record\n  6563\t  the conflict if the existing decisions do not determine a transition or a historical meaning. The seed-label question stays\n  6564\t  separate and unresolved. No selection-call design, no send.\n  6565\t\n  6566\t## D542 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the dependency stretch is closed with the separation recorded as a provisional candidate; the status is consolidated; nothing is sent (council consensus, reflection round 33)\n  6567\t\n  6568\t- **Done at $0 after D541** (`docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md` section 2.6): the\n  6569\t  package's own 287 tests run with the separated reading installed (`seam_plugin.py`): 285 pass as they are; the two others\n  6570\t  write by hand a row neither writer produces (one, the resume test, passes once its row is restated as a chosen dependency;\n  6571\t  the other holds D265 in its literal reading). In the 28 stored ledgers that hold only matching-era rows, the service shows\n  6572\t  what the candidate reads for all 399 questions with an edge (read at one far date). Three places where decisions and code\n  6573\t  part or the decisions are silent: an edge that would close a circle is dropped with a note where PRD 06 says refuse and ask\n  6574\t  for a correction; \"historical only\" has a reader and no writer; no decision says what happens to a later proposal with\n  6575\t  another direction for a pair already read.\n  6576\t- **The council's corrections:** a circle with stored work can arise at creation through an awaited question (`resolve_waiting`\n  6577\t  checks it and leaves the edge unbound); the census does hold theme-to-theme pairs both readers grant, so \"no pair names a\n  6578\t  theme\" was too broad. The suite under the seam is compatibility evidence, not a proof of every event.\n  6579\t- **Decided, citing D439:** the dependency stretch (D533 to D542) is closed. The separation is a provisional candidate, not\n  6580\t  sound for build; if the slice is reopened its review must settle the cycle through an awaited question at creation, closing\n  6581\t  behaviour, a theme shown twice, the historical readers and the label's meaning before any build. No selection call is\n  6582\t  designed and nothing is sent. Claude's proposed general rule (\"a contract that depends on an unbuilt piece is written only\n  6583\t  when that piece opens\") is **not** adopted: some such contracts decide whether the pieces can coexist, as the filing and\n  6584\t  reading conflict did; AGENTS §2 still requires the contracts complete before code. The next task is the consolidation of the\n  6585\t  status and the decision record (one next-task statement; production the default and both systems kept; D375 and D368 decided\n  6586\t  and awaiting implementation and acceptance). No open investigation outranks that closure on the choice between the systems;\n  6587\t  a new step worth a decision returns to the council under D439.\n  6588\t\n   121\t    views, archive = store_paths(case['draw'])\n   122\t    v = readonly(views)\n   123\t    j = v.execute('select * from judgements where view_id=? order by seq desc limit 1', (case['view_id'],)).fetchone()\n   124\t    a = readonly(archive)\n   125\t    row = a.execute('select request_json, response_json, answer_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1', (j['request_sha256'],)).fetchone()\n   126\t    return dict(j), json.loads(row['request_json']), json.loads(row['response_json']), json.loads(row['answer_json'])\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef without_previous(user):\n   130\t    \"\"\"The request's user text with the previous conclusion removed (council F: pair identical requests with and without it): the\n   131\t    \"[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] …\" block and the \"[Not shown: …; the previous conclusion carries them]\" line.\"\"\"\n   132\t    import re\n   133\t    start = user.find('\\n\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only]')\n   134\t    if start >= 0:\n   135\t        end = user.find('\\n\\nAnswer per the JSON schema.', start)\n   136\t        assert end > start, 'the previous conclusion block runs to the closing sentence'\n   137\t        user = user[:start] + user[end:]\n   138\t    return re.sub(r'^\\[Not shown: \\d+ more pieces in force, read in earlier judgements; the previous conclusion carries them\\]\\n?', '', user, flags=re.M)\n   139\t\n   140\t\n   141\tdef rebuild(stored_request, system_text, order=None, strip_previous=False):\n   142\t    \"\"\"The request as production builds it (model.build_request, key order and schema from code), with the given system text. With\n   143\t    `order`, the schema's properties are written in that order (the same fields and types; the model writes fields in this order).\"\"\"\n   144\t    from hivemind import config, model\n   145\t    from hivemind.views import judging\n   146\t    cfg = config.load(CONFIG)\n   147\t    user = stored_request['messages'][1]['content']\n   148\t    if strip_previous:\n   149\t        user = without_previous(user)\n   150\t    schema = judging.schema_for(cfg.rejudging.prompt_version)\n   151\t    if order is not None:\n   152\t        assert sorted(order) == sorted(schema['properties']), 'an order names exactly the schema fields'\n   917\t    return conn\n   918\t\n   919\t\n   920\tdef full_requests():\n   921\t    \"\"\"$0, council G: for each case, the stored final request rebuilt by the judge's own `build_prompt` on the store as it stood\n   922\t    (must equal the stored user text byte for byte), then the same request with every piece in force shown (no hidden line).\n   923\t    Writes fullcases.json with both user texts and the hidden count; only cases with at most 100 hidden pieces are kept.\"\"\"\n   924\t    from hivemind.views import judging, store\n   925\t    rows = json.loads((OUT / 'cases.json').read_text())\n   926\t    out, mismatched = [], []\n   927\t    original_view = judging.evidence_in_view\n   928\t    for case in rows:\n   929\t        judgement, request, _, _ = stored(case)\n   930\t        views, _ = store_paths(case['draw'])\n   931\t        conn = store_as_of(views, judgement['judgement_id'], judgement['seq'])\n   932\t        judging.evidence_in_view = original_view\n   933\t        _, user = judging.build_prompt(conn, case['view_id'], 'judging-v7')\n   934\t        stored_user = request['messages'][1]['content']\n   935\t        if user != stored_user:\n   936\t            mismatched.append(case['case'])\n   937\t            continue\n   938\t        shown, hidden = original_view(conn, case['view_id'])\n   939\t        if hidden > 100:\n   940\t            continue\n   941\t        judging.evidence_in_view = lambda c, v: (store.evidence_in_force(c, v), 0)\n   942\t        _, full_user = judging.build_prompt(conn, case['view_id'], 'judging-v7')\n   943\t        judging.evidence_in_view = original_view\n   944\t        out.append(dict(case, hidden=hidden, shown=len(shown), user_clipped=stored_user, user_full=full_user))\n   945\t    (OUT / 'fullcases.json').write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   946\t    print(f'{len(rows) - len(mismatched)} of {len(rows)} stored requests rebuilt byte for byte by build_prompt on the as-of store;',\n   947\t          'mismatch: ' + ', '.join(mismatched) if mismatched else '')\n   948\t    print(len(out), 'cases with at most 100 hidden pieces:', sum(c['role'] == 'target' for c in out), 'targets,',\n   949\t          sum(c['role'] == 'control' for c in out), 'controls; hidden pieces restored:', sum(c['hidden'] for c in out))\n   950\t\n   951\t\n   952\tdef fullscore(arms=('v7-fullprev', 'v7-fullnoprev')):\n    50\t- In `docs/DECISIONS-log.md`: D198 (search \"## D198\"), D260, D354, D543, D665, and D676–D688.\n    51\t- Data: `poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/` (probe, deck, marks and score files, `freshpool.json`, `window/`, `prodpath/`).\n    52\t- The judge's prompt and the code that builds its request: search `src/hivemind/` for \"Previous conclusion\" and `build_prompt`.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Questions\n    55\t1. **The judge.** Four angles failed (J2a, J2b, removing the previous conclusion, H1 the heading only). Is the remaining evidence a\n    56\t   quality defect worth taking to Alex as a D198 question?\n    57\t   - What is established: 0 of 13 move with the previous conclusion even on full evidence; 8 of 13 move without it, with 0 of 8\n    58\t     controls moving.\n    59\t   - What is not: net 4 jointly supported repairs against 5 required, and the frozen gold at 44.3 against 45.0, with d3-q17\n    60\t     regressed.\n    61\t   - If it is worth taking, what single test could decide it, given that the design has read every big numeric bet on this corpus\n    62\t     (the fresh census found 1 target against 8 needed)? Consider a fresh window, the whole-window judge-only replay (about $3.3 per\n    63\t     draw and arm), and D198 option 2 (a summary of the omitted evidence in place of the carried derivation). Give each test's cost,\n    64\t     and what result would move the decision.\n    65\t2. **Untested within D198:** moving the previous conclusion earlier in the request (named by reflection K). Is it a sourced lever, or\n    66\t   a guess after H1's failure?\n    67\t3. **Reading (c8).** Old's losses on the 32 matters are not reading losses (merge `RESULT.md`), and c8 adds about $24 to old's about\n    68\t   $9 over 82 days. Is there any reading quality target with a measurable effect on final answers? If not, should the line close?\n    69\t4. **Anything Claude has dropped:** a production defect inside old that is root-caused and in a module Alex has taken up. AGENTS §1\n    70\t   says such a defect is never parked. An example to check: the D260 stance-field order that never ran (D681).\n    71\t5. **The exit.** Name one recommendation and one test, or a close with its reopening conditions. What should go to Alex, and in what\n    72\t   form?\n    73\t\n    74\t## Deliver\n    75\t- Facts and hypotheses kept apart, with files and numbers cited.\n    76\t- Each claim says what would falsify it.\n    77\t- End with CONSENSUS-READY: <one line> or OPEN: <one line>.\n    78\t- Under 800 words.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20\\\")\ncases={i[\\\"case\\\"]:i for i in json.loads((p/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text())}\nprint(\\\"case keys\\\",sorted(next(iter(cases.values()))))\nmarks=json.loads((p/\\\"marks-full.json\\\").read_text())\nstored={v[\\\"case\\\"]:v[\\\"stored_rung\\\"] for v in marks.values() if \\\"stored_rung\\\" in v}\nfull=[i for i in json.loads((p/\\\"fullcases.json\\\").read_text()) if 1<=i[\\\"hidden\\\"]<=100]\nprint(\\\"full\\\",len(full))\nfor arm in (\\\"v7-fullprev\\\",\\\"v7-fullnoprev\\\"):\n hits=[]\n for x in full:\n  rs=[json.loads((p/\\\"probe\\\"/arm/(x[\\\"case\\\"]+f\\\"-{i}.json\\\")).read_text())[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"rung\\\"] for i in (1,2,3)]\n  source=stored[x[\\\"case\\\"]]\n  if sum(r\"'!=source for r in rs)>=2: hits.append((x[\"case\"],source,rs))\n print(arm,hits)\nfor arm in (\"v7\",\"J2a\",\"J2b\",\"v7-noprev\"):\n print(arm, [(f.name,json.loads(f.read_text())[\"answer\"][\"rung\"]) for f in sorted((p/\"goldprobe\"/arm).glob(\"*q17*\")) if \"d3-q17\" in f.name])\n'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c '\nimport json,pathlib\np=pathlib.Path(\\\"poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20\\\")\ncases={i[\\\"case\\\"]:i for i in json.loads((p/\\\"cases.json\\\").read_text())}\nprint(\\\"case keys\\\",sorted(next(iter(cases.values()))))\nmarks=json.loads((p/\\\"marks-full.json\\\").read_text())\nstored={v[\\\"case\\\"]:v[\\\"stored_rung\\\"] for v in marks.values() if \\\"stored_rung\\\" in v}\nfull=[i for i in json.loads((p/\\\"fullcases.json\\\").read_text()) if 1<=i[\\\"hidden\\\"]<=100]\nprint(\\\"full\\\",len(full))\nfor arm in (\\\"v7-fullprev\\\",\\\"v7-fullnoprev\\\"):\n hits=[]\n for x in full:\n  rs=[json.loads((p/\\\"probe\\\"/arm/(x[\\\"case\\\"]+f\\\"-{i}.json\\\")).read_text())[\\\"answer\\\"][\\\"rung\\\"] for i in (1,2,3)]\n  source=stored[x[\\\"case\\\"]]\n  if sum(r\"'!=source for r in rs)>=2: hits.append((x[\"case\"],source,rs))\n print(arm,hits)\nfor arm in (\"v7\",\"J2a\",\"J2b\",\"v7-noprev\"):\n print(arm, [(f.name,json.loads(f.read_text())[\"answer\"][\"rung\"]) for f in sorted((p/\"goldprobe\"/arm).glob(\"*q17*\")) if \"d3-q17\" in f.name])\n'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"case keys ['card', 'case', 'class', 'draw', 'label', 'mark', 'role', 'type', 'view_id']\nfull 21\nv7-fullprev []\nv7-fullnoprev [('T-old-1-Q28', 3, [1, 2, 2]), ('T-old-1-Q7', 4, [3, 3, 3]), ('T-old-2-Q16', 1, [3, 3, 1]), ('T-old-2-Q29', 3, [2, 2, 2]), ('T-old-3-Q14', 1, [2, 2, 1]), ('T-old-3-Q33', 3, [1, 2, 2]), ('T-old-3-Q37', 3, [2, 2, 2]), ('T-old-3-Q7', 4, [3, 3, 3])]\nv7 [('G-d3-q17-1.json', 4), ('G-d3-q17-2.json', 4), ('G-d3-q17-3.json', 4)]\nJ2a [('G-d3-q17-1.json', 5), ('G-d3-q17-2.json', 4), ('G-d3-q17-3.json', 4)]\nJ2b [('G-d3-q17-1.json', 5), ('G-d3-q17-2.json', 4), ('G-d3-q17-3.json', 4)]\nv7-noprev [('G-d3-q17-1.json', 5), ('G-d3-q17-2.json', 5), ('G-d3-q17-3.json', 5)]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'binding_obligation|material unsigned|annual profit|[0-9]%' src/hivemind/prompts/*v74i* src/hivemind/extraction.py | head -45; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '9413,9440p;10125,10150p;10299,10320p'; ls -l docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n*\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'binding_obligation|material unsigned|annual profit|[0-9]%' src/hivemind/prompts/*v74i* src/hivemind/extraction.py | head -45; nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '9413,9440p;10125,10150p;10299,10320p'; ls -l docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n*\"","aggregated_output":"src/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:4:- A material statement is one of four kinds. (1) The company's own figure, guidance or decision: \"same-store sales rose 4.2% in the quarter\"; \"management guided full-year revenue to $12–13 billion\"; \"the board approved a $10 billion buyback\". (2) A customer's, supplier's, competitor's or partner's action or reported figure with a size, date or name that bears on the company's demand, supply, input costs, competition, prices or products: \"the largest customer said it will cut orders by a fifth next year\"; \"a bank chose a rival's system\"; \"a software firm is integrating the company's model into its government systems\"; \"the main supplier said its capacity will double by 2027\"; \"a rival cut list prices 15% in Europe\"; \"the largest customer reported its order backlog doubled to $40 billion\". An action is a step the item reports as news: taken, decided or planned (an order, a contract, a selection, an integration under way, an expansion, a cut, a price change, a deployment plan). A party that already uses, hosts, runs or has built on the company's products, and the benefits it describes from that use (faster, cheaper, more accurate), describe an arrangement in place, which is background; its own revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amounts are figures under (2) (\"a hospital chain uses the company's scheduling software and reports shorter waits\"). (3) A named party's new claim or estimate about the company or its industry, with or without a figure, whether an analyst, a customer's or rival's executive or an official makes it: \"the CFO said plants built a decade ago still run at full capacity\"; \"an analyst raised next year's EPS estimate to $4.10\"; \"an analyst said the bank's loan losses next quarter will come in well above consensus\"; \"a short seller accused the company of overstating receivables by $2 billion\"; \"an analyst valued the shares at $80, 15 times next year's earnings of $5.30\". (4) A policy or regulatory decision or step, including one still in force that the item reports: \"the regulator approved the drug for a second indication\"; \"the government required licences for exports of the product\"; \"the regulator still bars sales of the drug in the country\".\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/role-v74i.txt:13:- Open a candidate only for one of four reasons, named in opens_as. main_driver: an annual quantity that carries the company's value (the segment that carries the business, gross margin, capital spending), whether or not the company guides it, or the date by which the generation of the company's own product that carries that quantity launches or starts shipping (a carmaker's next vehicle platform; not a feature, content or software update, regional service or variant of a product already on sale); the question's ranges settle it, not a guidance figure. Not every reported or guided line. industry_aggregate: one aggregate quantity for one calendar year, such as the combined capital spending of named companies. policy_stage: a stage of a policy process, with the authority that decides it named. binding_obligation: an obligation a universe company takes on in its own name: a guarantee or credit support for another party's debt, lease or revenue, financing it extends to others, a purchase commitment or a backstop of customers' capacity or revenue, whether or not the item gives its amount; or an equity stake whose size is stated and is not yet completed. Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations. Not yet signed: a yes/no question due on a day after the item by which the signing can be checked, at most 18 months out. Already taken on, as one deal or as a programme: a financing_amount question on the amount the obligation reaches at the company's next annual filing, settled by that filing's commitments note; the announcement itself is evidence to it.\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:22:ADMISSION_REASONS = ['main_driver', 'industry_aggregate', 'policy_stage', 'binding_obligation']\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:528:    if c['opens_as'] == 'binding_obligation':\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:629:        if c.get('measure') not in ('event', 'policy_event') and c.get('opens_as') != 'binding_obligation' \\\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/review-v74i.txt:4:- a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk (\"if demand slows it would hurt\"); a number does not lift a familiar position (\"the rival grocer has led this market for years and still holds 40%\"); it does not cover a dated forecast of a shortage, a price or demand (\"the steelmaker expects the shortage to peak next year and last until 2028\"), a competitor's newly reported share, volume or price in the company's market (\"the local rival now holds about half of the regional market, worth about $5 billion\"), nor a reported movement of a named price, rental rate, lead time or order book, even without a figure (\"rental rates for used trucks have been climbing this quarter\"); a general statement that demand stays strong or a product stays popular is not one;\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/review-v74i.txt:8:- a share-price move, an investor's position or trade, or the market value (\"shares fell 13% this month\"; \"he is short the stock\"); it does not cover the news behind the move;\nsrc/hivemind/prompts/review-v74i.txt:10:- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n  9413\t       each, and are scored on unread weeks from 07-20 up to 09-20, as far as the full exposure census supports. The exclusion list is frozen.\n  9414\t     - **The main quantity:** big matters served, paired per matter.\n  9415\t     - **Verdicts:**\n  9416\t       - **Practical lead:** a − b ≥ max(3, 15% of N) and a ≥ 2b. Every guardrail subgroup must meet its frozen minimum and pass under both split\n  9417\t         countings.\n  9418\t       - **Practical loss:** the mirror, or a guardrail breach confirmed under both countings.\n  9419\t       - **No practical winner, too small or invalid**, as written.\n  9420\t     - **Guardrails:** unsupported shares (figure and yes/no apart) and the not-worth-tracking share, each within 10 points of the old system's.\n  9421\t       D428's limits are printed beside them.\n  9422\t     - **Illustrative only:** a sign test and an interval.\n  9423\t     - **Frozen and hashed before the first send:** the matter list (blind), the credit rules (one cutoff per matter, the grouping of repeats,\n  9424\t       what counts as the same question), the controls, the versions and the rule.\n  9425\t  2. **What changes, explicitly:**\n  9426\t     - D548's use of D400's six lines as a release gate is superseded. The lines are reported on every ladder run.\n  9427\t     - The parts code decides stay hard: figure ranges meet end to end; the favourable end is stable; the due day is consistent at D400's 90%.\n  9428\t     - D431's frozen-reference reading of 07-01 to 07-14 is still produced and printed beside the comparison, not deciding. D665 supersedes D431\n  9429\t       on that point only.\n  9430\t     - Step 2's three checks stay as D427 and D431 set them.\n  9431\t     - Gate 2's unsupported lines become the guardrails, and its control line waits (D658).\n  9432\t     - Gate 4 folds in.\n  9433\t     - Gate 5 waits for a practical lead and Alex's word.\n  9434\t     - The absolute floors stay proposals, reported beside.\n  9435\t  3. **Back to Alex,** before any release engineering resumes: a practical lead (with the split cards for his spot check), a practical loss at\n  9436\t     once, no practical winner, too small or invalid, or no verdict by 2026-12-01.\n  9437\t- **Next:**\n  9438\t  - the comparison's design at $0: the exposure census, the frozen matter list and credit rules, the cards and controls, the replay plan and\n  9439\t    its spend guard;\n  9440\t  - council review;\n 10125\t## D681 · 2026-11-20 · Alex opens the hybrid system's build and test; phase 1 is a new judge version (J2) for the judge's reasoning errors\n 10126\t\n 10127\t- Alex, 2026-11-20, after the merge test (D680) and the finding that the old system loses on the 32 matters at opening and in the judge's\n 10128\t  reasoning, not in reading: \"不是聊了半天就是要合并两边最好的来提升系统吗？\"; then, on the proposal to fix the judge's reasoning errors\n 10129\t  first as a new judge version, with a council review and a test of a few cents: \"可以啊，你现在开始做hybrid system 的构建和测试，不要犯了和做新系统一样的错误到最后才发现问题\".\n 10130\t- Decided (his words): the hybrid system is built and tested. The judge (judging-v7, frozen by D354) may get a new version, J2, measured\n 10131\t  against v7. The frozen ruler is unchanged.\n 10132\t- The plan (`docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/PLAN.md`) guards against the new system's mistakes:\n 10133\t  - a change is accepted by its effect on final answers, read by blind readers;\n 10134\t  - an end-to-end slice runs in week 1;\n 10135\t  - the attainable verdict is computed first;\n 10136\t  - every line has a source;\n 10137\t  - the design uses the stored dev failures, and acceptance is on a fresh window.\n 10138\t- Attainable on the 32 matters (computed first):\n 10139\t  - the judge fix can add M08 and M14 to old's 10;\n 10140\t  - a release lead needs opening (phase 2);\n 10141\t  - with D382 applied to the hybrid's figure questions, the hybrid loses by construction. That choice is Alex's.\n 10142\t- First findings ($0, 2026-11-20):\n 10143\t  - 24 answers rejected by both readers. In about 16 of them the answer leaves its own reference's rung on a weak step: overlapping\n 10144\t    amounts added (6), a figure of another scope taken as the value (6), an adjustment with no basis (5).\n 10145\t  - The judge writes the rung first and the reference and implied outcome last, in all 48 stored answers read. `schema_for` appends\n 10146\t    the D260 stance fields to the end of the schema's properties, against its own comment: D260's intended order never ran.\n 10147\t- Correction: the merge-test report cited a planted reader control (C140) as an old-2 answer. Corrected in its `RESULT.md`.\n 10148\t- Record: `docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/` (PLAN.md, census/, DESIGN-J2.md).\n 10149\t\n 10150\t## D682 · 2026-11-20 · Under D681 (council): J2a and J2b retired; the carried previous conclusion is the lead mechanism; a separating test on complete evidence\n 10299\t  - The release bar stays.\n 10300\t- **To Alex, one recommendation:**\n 10301\t  - Keep poc-v118 as production and pause the hybrid's release line. The judge and reading fixes remain quality work.\n 10302\t  - Questions on key figures of other research-list companies are offered only if he wants those forecasts for their own value.\n 10303\t  - D543 applies, since another test would leave the decision unchanged.\n 10304\t- **Errors of mine, both corrected before council M closed:**\n 10305\t  - the first attainable check counted M12, M27 and M16 as gains within the rules without reading D248 boundary 1, D388 and D481;\n 10306\t  - the census section listed the categories without the decisions that bound them (AGENTS §2.4).\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    5840 Nov 20 12:59 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-brief.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    4445 Nov 20 13:01 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-claude.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff       0 Nov 20 12:59 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.md\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  640836 Nov 20 13:01 docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/council-n-codex.stream\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
