{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"**Keep poc-v118 in production, record Alex’s pause on the hybrid release, and close both quality experiments for now.** The judge sometimes repeats a bad forecast even when it has all the facts. That is worth recording for Alex. The current evidence supports neither changing what the judge carries forward nor paying for another test under D543. [D543](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6604) · [D688](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10299)\n\n**Judge.** With identical full evidence, keeping the previous conclusion moved 0/13 rejected forecasts. Removing it moved 8/13 and 0/8 controls. I reproduced those counts from the stored answers. Both readers supported only four net repairs against five required, and two repairs were the same capex question in different draws. The separate test that removed the conclusion from ordinary, clipped requests scored 44.3 versus 45.0. China share fell from 3/3 agreement to 0/3. Those results establish that the old conclusion can hold a bad forecast in place. A fresh test that repairs distinct forecasts and preserves supported answers would change the decision. [J2 results 4–7](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:280)\n\n- **Fresh window.** The stored pool had 27 unseen questions and only one eligible failure against eight needed. Reopen when an unseen window yields eight distinct eligible failures and matched supported controls. Three paired repeats would cost roughly **$0.17–$0.28** for 8–13 targets, plus **$0.67** for paired frozen checks. Preparing a new window costs extra. [Fresh test and census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:378)\n- **D198 option 2.** If the fresh pool qualifies, recommend asking Alex to approve one test of a source-checked summary of omitted facts in place of the old reasoning. The same judge calls would cost about **$0.85–$0.95** including the frozen checks, before summary preparation. A pass would show that the judge can keep the facts and drop the old mistake. A summary that loses a decisive fact or repeats an unsupported inference defeats that proposal. [D198](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2559) · [Option 2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:274)\n- **Whole-window replay.** **$6.60** for one paired draw, or **$19.80** for three, before summary costs. The stored replay reproduces 1,612/1,616 requests across 82 days. Use it after a candidate passes to see whether gains survive when each version builds its own history. A gain that disappears or breaks later answers ends the candidate. [Replay evidence](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-hybrid/DESIGN-J2.md:208)\n\n**Moving the old answer earlier** stays within D198. The code confirms it currently comes after the evidence and related forecasts. H1 changed its heading and repaired zero of three motivating cases. Placement remains a guess about which part of the request gets more weight. A position-only comparison showing supported repairs would overturn that assessment. [Request builder](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:121) · [H1 score](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/diag-score-H1.json)\n\n**Article reading.** Close c8. Its four supported answers cover two matters old already served. It adds about **$24 to $9** over 82 days. Reopen on a traced case where an article contains a decisive fact old failed to extract, c8 delivers it, and that fact alone can be tested against the same judge and question. [Merge results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-19-merge-council/RESULT.md:94)\n\n**Production defects.** D260 requires both explanations and specifies no output order. I verified that all 28 archived old-system answers in the probe wrote them last. J2a changed the order and moved the same two forecasts as the control. A repeatable gain attributable to order would reopen it. One actual omission remains under D368. Jev writes no links between questions for judging. I counted zero across 139 questions in the three old draws. That separately approved fix remains open. D538 showed that inserting a link as-is removes seven evidence links, and D542 records the unresolved design. [D260](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3049) · [D368](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3968) · [D538–D542](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6479)\n\n**Spend and exit.** Spendable headroom without Alex’s word is **$0**. Even ring-fencing every other authorized spend leaves only about $0.35 after phase1b. Counting the $2.13 merge spend that D679 also puts inside D439 gives about $41.78 before phase1. Send Alex a closure note and the conditions above. **Quality measure, proposed, not confirmed** — count net repairs on distinct final forecasts backed by both blind readers in two of three same-day pairs. Require four repairs at eight targets, no lost controls or extra refusals, and frozen agreement at least level with v7, including China share 3/3. [Spending record](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:8912) · [D679](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10097) · [Phase1b ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/hybrid-2026-11-20/ledger/phase1b.json)\n\nCONSENSUS-READY: Close both experiments now and return to Alex only when one bounded quality test can change a decision."}}
